var e={"if too many buckets are in use:":`如果 被占用的桶太多:`,"store key at bucket[hash(key) mod size]":`把 key 存到 bucket[hash(key) mod size]`,"make a table twice the size":`新建一张两倍大的表`,"for each key in the old table:":`对每个 旧表中的键:`,"put it at its bucket in the new one    // a different bucket":`把它放到新表中它的桶里    // 一个不同的桶`,"let the old table go":`释放旧表`,"How full":`有多满`,"A table filling up":`一张正在变满的表`,"The table in front has four buckets and three keys: cat in 0, fox in 1, dog in 2. It is three-quarters full.":`前面这张表有四个桶和三个键：cat 在 0，fox 在 1，dog 在 2。它已经四分之三满了。`,"How full a table is, keys divided by buckets, is its <strong>load factor</strong>. The row behind is a table twice the size, not yet in use.":`一张表有多满，即键数除以桶数，叫作它的<strong>负载因子</strong>。后面那一排是一张两倍大的表，还没有使用。`,"Buckets in use":`被占用的桶`,"Load factor":`负载因子`,"Collisions get likelier":`冲突越来越可能`,"Store bee. Its letters add up to 300, and 300 mod 4 is 0: where cat already is.":`存入 bee。它的字母加起来是 300，300 mod 4 是 0：cat 已经在那里了。`,"With three of four buckets taken, a new key has a three-in-four chance of colliding. Chains lengthen, probes wander, and lookups stop being O(1).":`四个桶占了三个，新键有四分之三的概率发生冲突。链变长，探测走得更远，查找也不再是 O(1)。`,"bee wants bucket 0 too":`bee 也想要 0 号桶`,"Past about 0.7 it is time to grow.":`超过大约 0.7，就该扩容了。`,"Move to a bigger table":`搬到更大的表`,Rehash:`再哈希`,"So the table grows: twice the buckets. But the keys cannot just be copied across. A key’s bucket depends on the table size, so every one has to be <strong>rehashed</strong>.":`所以表扩容了：桶数翻倍。但键不能直接复制过去。键的桶取决于表的大小，所以每个键都必须<strong>重新哈希</strong>。`,"cat: 312 mod 8 = 0. fox: 333 mod 8 = 5. dog: 314 mod 8 = 2. fox has moved from bucket 1 to bucket 5.":`cat：312 mod 8 = 0。fox：333 mod 8 = 5。dog：314 mod 8 = 2。fox 从 1 号桶搬到了 5 号桶。`,"Room again":`又有空间了`,"Now bee: 300 mod 8 = 4. Bucket 4 is free. The collision has gone, because the same keys are spread over twice as many buckets.":`现在是 bee：300 mod 8 = 4。4 号桶是空的。冲突消失了，因为同样的键分布在了两倍多的桶里。`,"Expensive, but rare":`昂贵，但少见`,"A resize touches every key, so that one insert costs O(n). But the table doubles each time, so resizes come twice as far apart as the table grows.":`一次扩容要处理每个键，所以那一次插入的代价是 O(n)。但表每次都翻倍，所以随着表变大，扩容之间的间隔也会翻倍。`,"Spread over all the inserts, the extra work averages out to a constant: the insert is O(1) <strong>amortized</strong>. It is the same argument as for a dynamic array.":`分摊到所有插入上，额外的工作平均下来是一个常数：插入的<strong>均摊</strong>代价是 O(1)。这和动态数组的道理一样。`,"O(1) amortized per insert, with an occasional O(n) pause.":`每次插入均摊 O(1)，偶尔有一次 O(n) 的停顿。`,"Half full: comfortable.":`半满：很宽松。`},t={"for each letter in word:":`对每个 word 中的字母:`,"if node has no child for it: add one":`如果 node 没有对应它的孩子: 添加一个`,"node ← that child":`node ← 那个孩子`,"mark node as the end of a word":`把 node 标记为一个词的结尾`,"if node has no child for it: return no":`如果 node 没有对应它的孩子: 返回 否`,"return whether node is marked":`返回 node 是否被标记`,"One letter per node":`每个节点一个字母`,"A <strong>trie</strong> (say “try”) stores words by spelling them out down a tree, one letter per node. A word is a path from the root.":`<strong>字典树</strong>（trie）把单词沿着一棵树逐个字母拼写出来存储，每个节点一个字母。一个单词就是从根出发的一条路径。`,"Here is CAT. The last letter is marked: that mark says “a word ends here”.":`这是 CAT。最后一个字母被标记了：这个标记的意思是“这里有一个单词结束”。`,"The way a dictionary’s page headers narrow down: C, then CA, then CAT.":`就像字典页眉一步步缩小范围：C，然后 CA，然后 CAT。`,"Words stored":`已存单词`,"Letters stored":`已存字母`,"of 3 written out":`/ 分开写需 3 个`,"Shared beginnings":`共用的开头`,"Add CAR. Walk down from the root: C is already there, and so is A. Only R is new.":`添加 CAR。从根往下走：C 已经在了，A 也在。只有 R 是新的。`,"Words that start the same way share their first nodes. The beginning is stored once, however many words use it.":`开头相同的单词共用最前面的节点。开头只存一次，不管有多少个单词用到它。`,"C: already here":`C：已经在了`,"A: already here":`A：已经在了`,"of 6 written out":`/ 分开写需 6 个`,"A word inside a word":`单词里的单词`,"Add DO and DOG. Nothing starts with D yet, so a new branch grows from the root.":`添加 DO 和 DOG。还没有以 D 开头的东西，所以从根长出一个新分支。`,"Both O and G are marked. DO ends at O even though the path carries on: the mark, not the end of the branch, is what makes it a word.":`O 和 G 都被标记了。DO 在 O 处结束，尽管路径还在继续：让它成为单词的是标记，而不是分支的尽头。`,"of 11 written out":`/ 分开写需 11 个`,"Look a word up":`查找一个单词`,"Is DOG in there? Follow D, O, G from the root. The path exists and ends on a marked node: yes.":`DOG 在里面吗？从根开始沿着 D、O、G 走。路径存在，并且结束在一个被标记的节点上：在。`,"Three letters, three steps. It makes no difference whether the trie holds four words or four million.":`三个字母，三步。字典树里存了四个单词还是四百万个，都没有区别。`,"O(length of the word). The number of words stored does not come into it.":`O(单词的长度)。存了多少个单词根本不影响。`,"G: a word ends here":`G：这里有一个单词结束`,"A path is not a word":`路径不等于单词`,"Is CA in there? C, then A: the path exists. But A is not marked, so no word ends there.":`CA 在里面吗？C，然后 A：路径存在。但 A 没有被标记，所以没有单词在那里结束。`,"CA is not a word in this trie. It is a <strong>prefix</strong>: the start of words that are.":`CA 不是这棵字典树里的单词。它是一个<strong>前缀</strong>：一些单词的开头。`,"A: no word ends here":`A：没有单词在这里结束`,"Everything that starts with…":`所有以……开头的`,"And that is what a trie is best at. Walk to the end of a prefix, and every word that starts with it is in the subtree below: CAT and CAR.":`而这正是字典树最擅长的。走到一个前缀的末尾，所有以它开头的单词都在下面的子树里：CAT 和 CAR。`,"A hash table can tell you whether CAT is stored. It cannot tell you what begins with CA without checking every key.":`哈希表能告诉你 CAT 有没有存。但它不检查每个键，就没法告诉你有哪些以 CA 开头。`,"Autocomplete, spell checkers, the routing tables that send packets across the internet.":`自动补全、拼写检查，还有把数据包送过互联网的路由表。`,"starts with CA":`以 CA 开头`,"The two words under C, A.":`C、A 下面的两个单词。`},n={"hash-tables":{"add up the codes of its letters":`把它各个字母的编码加起来`,"return the sum mod the number of buckets":`返回 总和 mod 桶的数量`,"return bucket[hash(key)] = key":`返回 bucket[hash(key)] = key`,"Finding a key":`查找一个键`,"Find without searching":`不用搜索就能找到`,"An array finds things instantly, but only by index: “what is in cell 4?”. Real questions are about <em>names</em>: “is cat in here?”. Answering that from a list means checking it item by item.":`数组能立刻找到东西，但只能按下标：“格子 4 里是什么？”。真正的问题是关于<em>名字</em>的：“cat 在这里吗？”。用列表回答这个问题，就得一项一项地检查。`,"A <strong>hash table</strong> gets the speed of an index for any kind of key. It starts as a plain array of <strong>buckets</strong>.":`<strong>哈希表</strong>让任何类型的键都能拥有下标的速度。它一开始只是一个由<strong>桶</strong>组成的普通数组。`,"Buckets looked in":`查看的桶数`,"In a plain list":`在普通列表中`,"worst case":`最坏情况`,"Seven buckets, all empty.":`七个桶，全是空的。`,"Turn the key into a number":`把键变成数字`,Hash:`哈希`,"The trick is a <strong>hash function</strong>: a fixed recipe that turns a key into a number. Here: add up the code numbers of the letters. For cat that is 99 + 97 + 116 = 312.":`诀窍是<strong>哈希函数</strong>：一个把键变成数字的固定方法。这里的方法是：把字母的编码加起来。cat 是 99 + 97 + 116 = 312。`,"There is no bucket 312, so keep only the remainder after dividing by the number of buckets: 312 mod 7 = <strong>4</strong>.":`没有 312 号桶，所以只保留除以桶数后的余数：312 mod 7 = <strong>4</strong>。`,"The one rule":`唯一的规则`,"The same key must always give the same number. Nothing random, nothing that changes.":`同一个键必须总是得到同一个数字。不能有随机的东西，也不能有会变的东西。`,"Store it there":`存到那里`,"The hash says bucket 4, so cat goes in bucket 4. No other bucket was even looked at.":`哈希说是 4 号桶，所以 cat 放进 4 号桶。其他桶连看都没看。`,"More keys":`更多的键`,"Each key is hashed in the same way and goes straight to its own bucket: dog to 6, owl to 2.":`每个键都用同样的方法哈希，直接进入自己的桶：dog 进 6，owl 进 2。`,"The buckets fill in no particular order. A hash table does not keep its keys sorted, or in the order they arrived.":`桶不按任何特定顺序填满。哈希表不会让键保持有序，也不会保持它们到达的顺序。`,"Look one up":`查找一个`,"Is dog in the table? Hash it again. The recipe has not changed, so the answer is 6 again. Look in bucket 6: there it is.":`dog 在表里吗？再哈希一次。方法没变，所以答案还是 6。看看 6 号桶：就在那里。`,"One bucket checked, however many keys are stored. That is the whole point.":`不管存了多少键，只检查了一个桶。这正是关键所在。`,"O(1) on average, for storing and for finding. A list would be O(n).":`存储和查找平均都是 O(1)。列表则是 O(n)。`,"dog: found":`dog：找到了`,"A miss is just as quick":`找不到也一样快`,"Is ant in the table? It hashes to 1, and bucket 1 is empty. If ant were stored, that is the only place it could be.":`ant 在表里吗？它哈希到 1，而 1 号桶是空的。如果存了 ant，它只可能在那里。`,"So it is not here. One look answered that too.":`所以它不在。看一次也回答了这个问题。`,"Two different keys can hash to the same bucket. What then is the next lesson.":`两个不同的键可能哈希到同一个桶。那时怎么办，是下一课的内容。`,"empty: not stored":`空：没有存`},"collision-handling":{"put with chaining(key):":`链地址法 put(key):`,"add key to the list at bucket[hash(key)]":`把 key 加到 bucket[hash(key)] 处的链表里`,"has with chaining(key):":`链地址法 has(key):`,"for each item in the list at bucket[hash(key)]:":`对每个 bucket[hash(key)] 处链表中的项:`,"if item = key: return yes":`如果 item = key: 返回 是`,"put with probing(key):":`线性探测 put(key):`,"while bucket[i] is taken:":`当 bucket[i] 已被占用:`,"i ← the next bucket":`i ← 下一个桶`,"has with probing(key):":`线性探测 has(key):`,"if bucket[i] = key: return yes":`如果 bucket[i] = key: 返回 是`,"How full, how far":`有多满，走多远`,"Two keys, one bucket":`两个键，一个桶`,"Store bee. Its letters add up to 300, and 300 mod 7 is 6. But dog is already in bucket 6.":`存入 bee。它的字母加起来是 300，300 mod 7 是 6。但 dog 已经在 6 号桶里了。`,"This is a <strong>collision</strong>. It is not a bug in the hash function: there are far more possible keys than buckets, so some are bound to share.":`这就是<strong>冲突</strong>。这不是哈希函数的 bug：可能的键远比桶多，所以总有一些要共用。`,"in 7 buckets":`在 7 个桶中`,"Places looked at":`查看的位置数`,"Bucket 6 is taken.":`6 号桶已被占用。`,Chaining:`链地址法`,"Fix one":`解法一`,"One answer: let a bucket hold more than one key. Each bucket is the head of a small linked list, and a colliding key is simply added to it.":`一种解法：让一个桶可以存多个键。每个桶都是一个小链表的头，冲突的键直接加进去。`,"bee joins the chain at bucket 6, behind dog.":`bee 加入 6 号桶的链，排在 dog 后面。`,"Looking along a chain":`沿着链查找`,"To find bee, hash it to bucket 6 as usual, then walk that bucket’s chain comparing keys: dog, no; bee, yes.":`要找 bee，照常把它哈希到 6 号桶，然后沿着这个桶的链逐个比较键：dog，不是；bee，是。`,"Only the keys that collided are checked, never the whole table.":`只检查发生冲突的键，从不检查整张表。`,"O(1) to reach the bucket, plus the length of its chain. Short chains keep it fast.":`到达桶是 O(1)，再加上链的长度。链短就快。`,"bee: found":`bee：找到了`,"Open addressing":`开放寻址`,"Fix two":`解法二`,"The other answer keeps one key per bucket, with no lists. Start again without bee, and store fox: it hashes to 4, where cat already is.":`另一种解法是每个桶只放一个键，不用链表。去掉 bee 重新开始，存入 fox：它哈希到 4，而 cat 已经在那里了。`,"With nowhere to chain, fox must find a different bucket.":`没有链可挂，fox 必须找另一个桶。`,"Bucket 4 is taken.":`4 号桶已被占用。`,"Probe for a free bucket":`探测空桶`,"The simplest rule is <strong>linear probing</strong>: try the next bucket along, and the next, until one is free. Bucket 5 is empty, so fox goes there.":`最简单的规则是<strong>线性探测</strong>：试下一个桶，再下一个，直到找到空的。5 号桶是空的，所以 fox 放在那里。`,"It is not where its hash said. That is fine, as long as lookups follow the same rule.":`它不在哈希说的位置。这没关系，只要查找时遵循同样的规则就行。`,"next free bucket":`下一个空桶`,"Find it the same way":`用同样的方法查找`,"Looking for fox: hash to 4, find cat, not it. Move along to 5: fox. An empty bucket would have meant “not stored”.":`查找 fox：哈希到 4，发现是 cat，不是它。往后移到 5：fox。如果遇到空桶，就意味着“没有存”。`,"Either way, the fuller the table, the longer the chains or the probing. So tables watch how full they are, and move everything into a bigger array before it hurts.":`无论哪种方法，表越满，链就越长，探测也越久。所以哈希表会关注自己有多满，在出问题之前把所有东西搬到一个更大的数组里。`,"Keep it under about two-thirds full. Past that, grow and re-hash every key.":`保持在大约三分之二满以下。超过了就扩容，并重新哈希每个键。`,"fox: found":`fox：找到了`,"Four of seven buckets used.":`七个桶用了四个。`},resizing:e,"sets-and-maps":{"seen ← an empty set":`seen ← 一个空集合`,"for each animal that goes by:":`对每个 经过的动物:`,"if seen has it: skip it":`如果 seen 里有它: 跳过`,"else: add it to seen":`否则: 把它加进 seen`,"count ← an empty map":`count ← 一个空映射`,"if count has it: count[animal] ← count[animal] + 1":`如果 count 里有它: count[animal] ← count[animal] + 1`,"else: count[animal] ← 1":`否则: count[animal] ← 1`,"A set":`集合`,"You rarely build a hash table yourself. You use the two things made from one. The first is a <strong>set</strong>: a collection of keys and nothing else.":`你很少需要自己实现哈希表。你用的是用哈希表做成的两样东西。第一样是<strong>集合</strong>：只有键、别无他物的一组东西。`,"A set answers one question, fast: “is this in here?”. It has no order and no positions.":`集合能快速回答一个问题：“这个在里面吗？”。它没有顺序，也没有位置。`,"This is a":`这是一个`,set:`集合`,"It holds":`它存着`,"Is it in?":`在里面吗？`,"Has a dog been seen? Hash the key, look in its bucket: yes.":`见过 dog 吗？哈希这个键，看它的桶：见过。`,"That is the lookup from the hash table lesson, and it is the whole of what a set is for.":`这就是哈希表那一课里的查找，也是集合的全部用途。`,"O(1) on average, where searching a list is O(n).":`平均 O(1)，而在列表里搜索是 O(n)。`,"No duplicates":`没有重复`,"Add cat again. It hashes to the bucket where cat already is, so there is nothing to do.":`再加一次 cat。它哈希到 cat 已经在的那个桶，所以什么都不用做。`,"A set holds each key once, however often it is added. Pour a list into a set and the repeats are gone.":`集合中每个键只存一次，不管加了多少次。把一个列表倒进集合，重复的就没了。`,"already here":`已经在这里`,"Still three keys.":`仍然是三个键。`,"A map":`映射`,"The second is a <strong>map</strong> (also called a dictionary): the same table, with a <strong>value</strong> kept beside each key.":`第二样是<strong>映射</strong>（也叫字典）：同样的表，只是每个键旁边还存着一个<strong>值</strong>。`,"The key says which bucket. The value rides along with it. Here each animal carries how many times it has been seen.":`键决定放在哪个桶。值跟着它一起走。这里每种动物都带着它被见到的次数。`,map:`映射`,"Update a value":`更新一个值`,Map:`映射`,"Another dog goes by. Find dog by its key, read its value, write back one more.":`又一只 dog 经过。按它的键找到 dog，读出它的值，写回多一的数。`,"Only the value changed. The key is still in the same bucket, because its hash has not changed.":`只有值变了。键还在同一个桶里，因为它的哈希没有变。`,"Count anything":`什么都能数`,"An ant, never seen before: it goes in with a count of 1. Those two cases, “seen it” and “new”, are the whole loop.":`一只 ant，以前从没见过：它以计数 1 加入。“见过”和“新的”这两种情况，就是整个循环。`,"This is how words in a book are counted, how votes are tallied, how duplicates are found. One pass over the data, one quick step per item.":`数一本书里的词、统计选票、找出重复项，都是这样做的。数据过一遍，每项一步快速操作。`,"Need “have I seen this?”: a set. Need “what goes with this?”: a map.":`需要“我见过这个吗？”：用集合。需要“这个对应什么？”：用映射。`},"bloom-filters":{"for each hash function h:":`对每个 哈希函数 h:`,"if bits[h(key)] = 0: return no     // certain":`如果 bits[h(key)] = 0: 返回 否     // 确定`,"return maybe                           // probably":`返回 可能                           // 很可能`,"The filter":`过滤器`,"A set that forgets the keys":`一个会忘记键的集合`,"A hash set answers “is this in here?” exactly, but it has to store every key. A <strong>Bloom filter</strong> answers the same question in a sliver of the memory, by storing no keys at all: only a row of bits.":`哈希集合能准确回答“这个在里面吗？”，但它得存下每个键。<strong>布隆过滤器</strong>只用一小部分内存就能回答同样的问题，因为它根本不存键：只存一排位。`,"The price is that it is sometimes wrong, in one direction only.":`代价是它有时会出错，而且只会错向一个方向。`,Added:`已添加`,"Asked about":`被询问`,"Adding sets a few bits":`添加就是设置几个位`,"To add cat, run it through two different hash functions. They give 1 and 4. Set those two bits to 1.":`要添加 cat，就让它通过两个不同的哈希函数。它们给出 1 和 4。把这两个位设为 1。`,"Nothing else about cat is kept.":`关于 cat 的其他信息都不保留。`,"add cat":`添加 cat`,"Bits are shared":`位是共用的`,"Add dog: its two hashes are 4 and 6. Bit 4 was already set by cat. That is fine: a bit only records that <em>something</em> set it.":`添加 dog：它的两个哈希值是 4 和 6。第 4 位已经被 cat 设置过了。这没关系：一个位只记录<em>有东西</em>设置过它。`,"add dog":`添加 dog`,"A zero means no":`0 表示不在`,"Is bee in the set? Its hashes are 3 and 6. Bit 3 is 0. If bee had ever been added, that bit would be 1.":`bee 在集合里吗？它的哈希值是 3 和 6。第 3 位是 0。如果 bee 曾经被添加过，这个位就会是 1。`,"So bee is <strong>definitely not</strong> there. A Bloom filter never says no by mistake.":`所以 bee <strong>肯定不</strong>在里面。布隆过滤器从不会错误地说“不在”。`,"0: never added":`0：从未添加`,"All ones means maybe":`全是 1 表示可能`,"Is owl in the set? Its hashes are 1 and 6. Both bits are 1, so the filter says yes. But owl was never added: cat set bit 1 and dog set bit 6.":`owl 在集合里吗？它的哈希值是 1 和 6。两个位都是 1，所以过滤器说在。但 owl 从没被添加过：第 1 位是 cat 设置的，第 6 位是 dog 设置的。`,"This is a <strong>false positive</strong>. A yes only ever means “maybe”.":`这就是<strong>假阳性</strong>。“在”永远只意味着“可能在”。`,"both set: maybe":`都已设置：可能`,maybe:`可能`,"Wrong this time.":`这次错了。`,"A cheap first check":`便宜的初步检查`,"That one-sided error is very useful. Put the filter in front of something slow, such as a disk or a network call. A “no” skips the slow step entirely; a “maybe” goes on to the real check.":`这种单向的错误非常有用。把过滤器放在慢的东西前面，比如磁盘或网络调用。“不在”就完全跳过慢的步骤；“可能”才继续做真正的检查。`,"More bits and more hash functions make false positives rarer. Keys cannot be removed, since a bit may belong to several.":`位越多、哈希函数越多，假阳性就越少。键不能删除，因为一个位可能属于好几个键。`,"Databases checking whether a file could hold a key; browsers checking a URL against a list of unsafe sites.":`数据库检查一个文件是否可能包含某个键；浏览器把网址和不安全网站列表比对。`,"Three bits stand for two keys of any size.":`三个位代表了两个任意大小的键。`},"binary-trees":{"left       // another node, or nothing":`left       // 另一个节点，或者空`,"right      // another node, or nothing":`right      // 另一个节点，或者空`,"root       // the one node with no parent":`root       // 唯一没有父节点的节点`,"This tree":`这棵树`,"One node, two children":`一个节点，两个孩子`,"A linked-list node points at one other node. Give a node <strong>two</strong> pointers, <em>left</em> and <em>right</em>, and the list becomes a tree.":`链表的节点指向另一个节点。给节点<strong>两个</strong>指针，<em>left</em> 和 <em>right</em>，链表就变成了树。`,"A is the <strong>root</strong>: the one node nothing points at. B and C are its <strong>children</strong>, and A is their <strong>parent</strong>.":`A 是<strong>根</strong>：唯一没有东西指向的节点。B 和 C 是它的<strong>孩子</strong>，A 是它们的<strong>父节点</strong>。`,"A family tree drawn with the oldest ancestor at the top.":`一张家谱，最老的祖先画在最上面。`,"the root":`根`,Leaves:`叶子`,"no children":`没有孩子`,"longest way down":`最长的向下路径`,"It keeps branching":`它不断分叉`,"Each child can have two children of its own, and so on down.":`每个孩子还可以有自己的两个孩子，一直往下。`,"A node with no children is a <strong>leaf</strong>. D, E, F and G are the leaves here: every way down from the root ends at one.":`没有孩子的节点叫<strong>叶子</strong>。这里 D、E、F 和 G 是叶子：从根往下的每条路都终止于一片叶子。`,"Depth and height":`深度与高度`,Measure:`测量`,"A node’s <strong>depth</strong> is how many branches lie between it and the root. The root is at depth 0, its children at depth 1.":`节点的<strong>深度</strong>是它和根之间有多少条树枝。根的深度是 0，它的孩子的深度是 1。`,"The tree’s <strong>height</strong> is the depth of its deepest leaf: here, 2. Most of what a tree costs to use depends on its height.":`树的<strong>高度</strong>是它最深的叶子的深度：这里是 2。使用一棵树的大部分代价都取决于它的高度。`,"Trees inside trees":`树中有树`,"Look only at B and everything below it. That is a tree too, with B as its root: a <strong>subtree</strong>.":`只看 B 和它下面的一切。那也是一棵树，以 B 为根：一棵<strong>子树</strong>。`,"Every node is the root of its own subtree. This is why so much tree code is recursive: do the job for a node, then for its left subtree, then its right.":`每个节点都是它自己那棵子树的根。这就是为什么那么多处理树的代码都是递归的：为一个节点做事，然后为它的左子树做，再为它的右子树做。`,"a subtree":`一棵子树`,"Counting only the subtree under B.":`只计算 B 下面的子树。`,"How much fits":`能装多少`,Growth:`增长`,"Every level can hold twice as many nodes as the one above: 1, 2, 4, 8. One more level roughly doubles the whole tree.":`每一层能装的节点数是上一层的两倍：1、2、4、8。多一层，整棵树大约翻一倍。`,"So a full tree of height 3 holds 15 nodes, and one of height 20 holds over two million. A lot of data is only a few steps from the root.":`所以高度为 3 的满树能装 15 个节点，高度为 20 的能装两百多万个。大量数据离根只有几步之遥。`,"n nodes can fit in a height of about log₂ n. That is where tree speed comes from.":`n 个节点可以装进大约 log₂ n 的高度。树的速度就来自这里。`,"Not always tidy":`不总是整齐的`,"Nothing says a binary tree must be full. “Binary” only promises <em>at most</em> two children.":`没有规定二叉树必须是满的。“二叉”只保证<em>最多</em>两个孩子。`,"This one has five nodes and is as tall as the fifteen-node tree was. Taken to the extreme, with one child everywhere, a tree is just a linked list.":`这棵树有五个节点，却和那棵十五个节点的树一样高。走到极端，每处都只有一个孩子，树就只是一个链表。`,"Same height, a third of the nodes.":`同样的高度，三分之一的节点。`},"tree-traversals":{"if node is nothing: return":`如果 node 为空: 返回`,"visit node             // here: pre-order":`访问 node             // 在这里：前序`,"visit node             // here: in-order":`访问 node             // 在这里：中序`,"visit node             // here: post-order":`访问 node             // 在这里：后序`,"put root in a queue":`把 root 放进一个队列`,"take a node from the front, visit it":`从队首取出一个节点，访问它`,"put its children at the back":`把它的孩子放到队尾`,"Orders of visiting":`访问顺序`,"Visit every node":`访问每个节点`,"A list has one obvious order to read it in. A tree does not: at every node there are two ways to go.":`列表只有一种显而易见的读法。树没有：在每个节点上都有两条路可走。`,"A <strong>traversal</strong> is a rule for visiting every node exactly once. There are four standard ones, and they differ only in <em>when</em> each node gets its turn.":`<strong>遍历</strong>是让每个节点恰好被访问一次的规则。标准的有四种，它们唯一的区别是每个节点<em>什么时候</em>轮到。`,"Pre-order":`前序`,"In-order":`中序`,"Post-order":`后序`,"Level-order":`层序`,"Seven nodes, many possible orders.":`七个节点，可能的顺序有很多。`,"Depth first":`深度优先`,"Walk the tree depth first: down the left as far as possible, back up, then down the right.":`深度优先地走这棵树：沿左边尽量往下走，退回来，再往右边下去。`,"<strong>Pre-order</strong> counts a node the moment the walk first reaches it, before either subtree. Parents always come before their children.":`<strong>前序</strong>在第一次走到一个节点时就计数它，早于它的两棵子树。父节点总是排在孩子前面。`,"Good for":`适用于`,"Copying a tree, or writing it out: you meet each parent before you need to attach its children.":`复制一棵树，或者把它写出来：在需要挂上孩子之前，你已经先遇到了它们的父节点。`,"The walk is exactly the same. Watch the cursor: it takes the same path round the tree.":`走法完全一样。看着游标：它绕着树走的是同一条路。`,"<strong>In-order</strong> counts a node on the way back up from its left subtree, before going down the right: left, node, right.":`<strong>中序</strong>在从左子树返回的路上计数一个节点，然后才往右下去：左、节点、右。`,"A binary search tree: in-order visits its values from smallest to largest.":`二叉搜索树：中序遍历会从小到大访问它的值。`,"Same walk a third time. <strong>Post-order</strong> counts a node only when the walk is leaving it for good, after both subtrees are done.":`第三次走同样的路。<strong>后序</strong>只在彻底离开一个节点时才计数它，也就是两棵子树都处理完之后。`,"Children always come before their parent, and the root comes last.":`孩子总是排在父节点前面，根排在最后。`,"Deleting a tree, or adding up sizes: a node is handled once everything under it is finished.":`删除一棵树，或者累加大小：一个节点要等它下面的一切都处理完才处理。`,"Breadth first":`广度优先`,"The fourth order does not follow the branches at all. It reads the tree like a page: top level first, each level left to right.":`第四种顺序完全不沿着树枝走。它像读一页书那样读树：先读最上层，每层从左到右。`,"It needs a <strong>queue</strong> to remember whose children are next, where the depth-first walks use the call stack.":`它需要一个<strong>队列</strong>来记住接下来轮到谁的孩子，而深度优先的走法用的是调用栈。`,"Finding the nearest thing to the root: it reaches closer nodes before farther ones.":`找离根最近的东西：它会先到达较近的节点，再到达较远的。`},"lowest-common-ancestor":{"if node is nothing, or is p, or is q:":`如果 node 为空，或者是 p，或者是 q:`,"if both found something:":`如果 两边都找到了东西:`,"return node            // p and q are on different sides":`返回 node            // p 和 q 在不同的两边`,"return whichever one did":`返回 找到东西的那一边`,"Where two paths join":`两条路在哪里汇合`,"In a family tree, who is the closest ancestor two people share? In a folder tree, what is the smallest folder that contains two files?":`在家谱里，两个人共有的最近的祖先是谁？在文件夹树里，同时包含两个文件的最小文件夹是哪个？`,"Both are the same question: the <strong>lowest common ancestor</strong> of two nodes.":`两个都是同一个问题：两个节点的<strong>最近公共祖先</strong>。`,"The two nodes":`这两个节点`,"Lowest common ancestor":`最近公共祖先`,Ancestors:`祖先`,"A node’s ancestors are everything on the way from it up to the root. For D that is B, then A.":`一个节点的祖先，是从它往上到根的路上的一切。D 的祖先是 B，然后是 A。`,"Every node counts as an ancestor of itself.":`每个节点都算是它自己的祖先。`,"D’s ancestors: D, B, A.":`D 的祖先：D、B、A。`,"The first one they share":`它们共有的第一个`,"Take D and G. D’s ancestors are D, B, A. G’s are G, C, A. Going up from each, the first node on both lists is A.":`取 D 和 G。D 的祖先是 D、B、A。G 的是 G、C、A。从各自往上走，第一个同时出现在两个列表里的节点是 A。`,"D is in A’s left subtree and G in its right. That is the test: the lowest common ancestor is where the two nodes fall on <em>different sides</em>.":`D 在 A 的左子树里，G 在右子树里。这就是判断方法：最近公共祖先就是两个节点落在<em>不同两边</em>的地方。`,"they split here":`它们在这里分开`,"D and G":`D 和 G`,"Lower down":`再往下`,"Now D and E. Both are under B, one on each side of it. So B is their lowest common ancestor. A is also a common ancestor, but it is not the lowest.":`现在是 D 和 E。两个都在 B 下面，一边一个。所以 B 是它们的最近公共祖先。A 也是公共祖先，但不是最近的。`,"D and E":`D 和 E`,"One above the other":`一个在另一个上面`,"Edge case":`边界情况`,"What about B and E? E is underneath B, so B is an ancestor of both, itself included. The answer is B.":`B 和 E 呢？E 在 B 下面，所以 B 是两者的祖先，包括它自己。答案是 B。`,"The search stops as soon as it reaches either node: whatever is below it cannot change the answer.":`搜索一到达其中任何一个节点就停止：它下面的东西都不会改变答案。`,"its own ancestor":`是它自己的祖先`,"B and E":`B 和 E`,"One walk of the tree":`走一遍树`,"A single depth-first walk answers it: each node reports upward whether one of the two was found beneath it, and the first node to hear from both sides is the answer.":`一次深度优先遍历就能回答：每个节点向上报告它下面是否找到了两者之一，第一个从两边都收到消息的节点就是答案。`,"In a binary search tree it is easier still: walk down from the root until the two values fall on opposite sides.":`在二叉搜索树里就更简单了：从根往下走，直到两个值落在相反的两边。`,"O(n) in any tree, O(height) in a search tree.":`任何树都是 O(n)，搜索树是 O(高度)。`},"binary-search-trees":{"if node is nothing: return not found":`如果 node 为空: 返回 未找到`,"if x = node.value: return node":`如果 x = node.value: 返回 node`,"if x < node.value: return search(node.left, x)":`如果 x < node.value: 返回 search(node.left, x)`,"return search(node.right, x)":`返回 search(node.right, x)`,"if node is nothing: return a new node holding x":`如果 node 为空: 返回 一个存放 x 的新节点`,"if x < node.value: node.left ← insert(node.left, x)":`如果 x < node.value: node.left ← insert(node.left, x)`,"else: node.right ← insert(node.right, x)":`否则: node.right ← insert(node.right, x)`,"Smaller left, bigger right":`左边小，右边大`,"A <strong>binary search tree</strong> is a binary tree with one rule. At every node, everything in its left subtree is smaller and everything in its right subtree is bigger.":`<strong>二叉搜索树</strong>是带有一条规则的二叉树。在每个节点上，左子树里的一切都更小，右子树里的一切都更大。`,"Check it: left of 50 are 20, 30, 40. Right of it are 60, 70, 80. The same holds at 30 and at 70.":`检查一下：50 的左边是 20、30、40。右边是 60、70、80。在 30 和 70 上也是如此。`,"The rule covers whole subtrees, not just the two children.":`这条规则管的是整棵子树，而不只是两个孩子。`,"Nodes in the tree":`树中的节点`,"Nodes looked at":`查看的节点`,"To find 60, start at the root and compare. 60 is bigger than 50, so it can only be on the right: the entire left half is ruled out at once.":`要找 60，就从根开始比较。60 比 50 大，所以它只可能在右边：整个左半边一下子就被排除了。`,"60 is smaller than 70, so go left. There it is. Three nodes looked at, out of seven.":`60 比 70 小，所以往左走。就在那里。七个节点只看了三个。`,"One comparison per level: O(height). In a well-shaped tree that is O(log n).":`每层比较一次：O(高度)。在形状好的树里，那就是 O(log n)。`,"60 > 50: go right":`60 > 50：往右`,"60 < 70: go left":`60 < 70：往左`,"found 60":`找到 60`,"It is binary search, with the halving built into the shape.":`这就是二分查找，只是对半分已经内置在形状里了。`,"A miss":`找不到`,"Look for 45. Left at 50, right at 30, right at 40, and there is no node there.":`找 45。在 50 往左，在 30 往右，在 40 往右，那里没有节点。`,"That empty place is the only one 45 could have been in, so it is not in the tree. No need to look anywhere else.":`那个空位是 45 唯一可能在的地方，所以它不在树里。不用再去别处找了。`,"45 < 50: go left":`45 < 50：往左`,"45 > 30: go right":`45 > 30：往右`,"45 > 40: go right":`45 > 40：往右`,"nothing here":`这里什么都没有`,"Inserting is searching, then filling the gap. The search for 45 ended at an empty place below 40: that is exactly where 45 belongs.":`插入就是先搜索，再填空。搜索 45 停在了 40 下面的一个空位：45 正应该放在那里。`,"A new node always goes in as a leaf. Nothing else has to move.":`新节点总是作为叶子放进去。其他什么都不用动。`,"In order means sorted":`中序就是有序`,Property:`性质`,"Walk the tree in-order: left subtree, node, right subtree. Because smaller is always left, the values come out from smallest to largest.":`中序遍历这棵树：左子树、节点、右子树。因为小的总在左边，值就会从小到大地出来。`,"So a binary search tree is a sorted collection that is also quick to search and to add to.":`所以二叉搜索树是一个有序的集合，同时搜索和添加都很快。`,"It depends on the shape":`这取决于形状`,"Now build a tree by inserting 10, 20, 30, 40 in that order. Each is bigger than everything before it, so each goes to the right of the last.":`现在按 10、20、30、40 的顺序插入来建一棵树。每个都比之前的所有值大，所以每个都放在上一个的右边。`,"It obeys the rule, and it is useless: a linked list with extra pointers. Searching it is O(n).":`它遵守规则，但毫无用处：一个多带了指针的链表。在它里面搜索是 O(n)。`,"Keeping a tree short however the values arrive is what balanced trees are for.":`不管值以什么顺序到来，都让树保持矮，这正是平衡树的用途。`,"Finding 40 looks at every node.":`找 40 要看每一个节点。`},"bst-deletion":{"if it has no children:":`如果 它没有孩子:`,"unhook it":`把它解开`,"else if it has one child:":`否则，如果它有一个孩子:`,"put that child in its place":`让那个孩子顶替它的位置`,"next ← the smallest node in its right subtree":`next ← 它右子树中最小的节点`,"copy next's value into the node":`把 next 的值复制到这个节点里`,"delete next              // which has at most one child":`删除 next              // 它最多只有一个孩子`,"Removing a node":`删除一个节点`,"Three cases":`三种情况`,"Taking a value out of a binary search tree is harder than putting one in, because the hole has to be filled without breaking the order.":`从二叉搜索树里取出一个值，比放进一个值更难，因为必须在不破坏顺序的情况下填上空位。`,"What to do depends on how many children the node has: none, one or two.":`怎么做取决于这个节点有几个孩子：零个、一个还是两个。`,"This case":`这种情况`,"No children":`没有孩子`,"Case one":`情况一`,"20 is a leaf. Nothing hangs below it, so nothing can be disturbed: unhook it from its parent and it is gone.":`20 是叶子。它下面什么都没挂，所以什么都不会受影响：把它从父节点上解开，它就没了。`,"20 unhooked":`20 已解开`,"One child":`一个孩子`,"Case two":`情况二`,"60 has a single child, 65. Everything under 60 already belongs on that side of 70, so the child can simply move up into its place.":`60 只有一个孩子，65。60 下面的一切本来就属于 70 的这一边，所以这个孩子可以直接上移到它的位置。`,"takes 60’s place":`顶替 60 的位置`,"one child":`一个孩子`,"Two children: find a stand-in":`两个孩子：找一个替身`,"Case three":`情况三`,"Now delete 50, the root. It has two subtrees and only one place for them to hang.":`现在删除根 50。它有两棵子树，却只有一个地方能挂。`,"So the node is kept and its <em>value</em> replaced, with the next value up in order: go right once, then left as far as possible. That is 65. It is bigger than everything on the left and smaller than everything else on the right.":`所以保留这个节点，替换它的<em>值</em>，换成按顺序紧接着的下一个值：往右走一步，再尽量往左走。那是 65。它比左边的一切都大，又比右边其余的一切都小。`,"right once":`往右一步`,"then left to the end":`再一直往左`,"two children":`两个孩子`,"65 takes the root’s place. The stand-in was itself easy to remove: being the leftmost of its subtree, it had no left child, so it was one of the first two cases.":`65 顶替了根的位置。替身本身很容易删除：作为它所在子树最左边的节点，它没有左孩子，所以属于前两种情况之一。`,"Still in order":`仍然有序`,"Walk what is left in order: 30, 40, 65, 70, 80. Still sorted, so it is still a search tree.":`按中序走一遍剩下的：30、40、65、70、80。仍然有序，所以它仍然是搜索树。`,"Each case walked at most one path down the tree.":`每种情况最多沿树往下走一条路径。`,"O(height), like search and insert.":`O(高度)，和搜索、插入一样。`,"Three removed, order intact.":`删除了三个，顺序完好。`},"balanced-trees":{"insert x as in any search tree":`像在任何搜索树中一样插入 x`,"on the way back up, at each node:":`在返回的路上，在每个节点:`,"if one side is two taller than the other:":`如果 一边比另一边高出两层:`,"rotate the node towards the short side":`把节点往矮的一边旋转`,"node.right ← child.left      // the middle subtree changes sides":`node.right ← child.left      // 中间的子树换到另一边`,"return child                 // it takes the node's place":`返回 child                 // 它顶替这个节点的位置`,"How tall":`有多高`,"A lopsided tree":`一棵歪斜的树`,"Insert 10, 20, 30 into a search tree and it comes out as a chain. It is as tall as it could possibly be.":`把 10、20、30 插入一棵搜索树，它就成了一条链。它已经高到不能再高了。`,"Everything a search tree does costs its height, so this is the shape to avoid. A <strong>balanced</strong> tree fixes its own shape as it grows.":`搜索树做的每件事都取决于它的高度，所以这正是要避免的形状。<strong>平衡</strong>树会在长大的过程中自己调整形状。`,"right side is 2 taller":`右边高出 2 层`,"Shortest possible":`最矮可能的高度`,"A rotation":`旋转`,Repair:`修复`,"The fix is a <strong>rotation</strong>. 20 moves up to become the root, and 10 comes down to be its left child.":`修复方法是<strong>旋转</strong>。20 上移成为根，10 下来成为它的左孩子。`,"The order is untouched: 10 is still left of 20, and 30 is still right of it. It is the same search tree, one level shorter.":`顺序没有被破坏：10 仍在 20 的左边，30 仍在它的右边。它还是同一棵搜索树，只是矮了一层。`,"A rotation rewrites a few pointers. It is O(1), whatever the size of the tree.":`一次旋转只改写几个指针。它是 O(1)，不管树有多大。`,"Insert, then check":`插入，然后检查`,"Carry on: insert 40, then 50. Each goes in at the bottom right, as usual.":`继续：插入 40，然后 50。每个都照常放到右下方。`,"After 50, look at 30. Its right side is two levels tall and its left side is empty: out of balance.":`插入 50 之后，看看 30。它的右边有两层高，左边是空的：失去平衡了。`,"Repair where it broke":`在出问题的地方修复`,"Rotate at 30, the lowest node that is out of balance. 40 moves up into its place, with 30 and 50 either side.":`在 30 处旋转，它是最低的失衡节点。40 上移到它的位置，30 和 50 分在两边。`,"Only that corner of the tree changed. Everything above it is as it was.":`只有树的那个角落变了。它上面的一切都和原来一样。`,"A subtree changes sides":`一棵子树换边`,"Insert 60, and now the root itself is lopsided: one level on its left, three on its right. Rotate at 20.":`插入 60，现在根本身歪了：左边一层，右边三层。在 20 处旋转。`,"40 becomes the root. It already had a left child, 30, and that place is now needed for 20. So 30 moves across to hang under 20, which is where a value between 20 and 40 belongs.":`40 成为根。它原本就有一个左孩子 30，而那个位置现在需要留给 20。所以 30 挪过去挂在 20 下面，那正是介于 20 和 40 之间的值该在的地方。`,"Short, whatever arrives":`不管来什么，都保持矮`,"Six values went in already sorted, the worst case for a plain search tree, and the result is as short as a tree of six can be.":`六个值按已排好的顺序放进来，这对普通搜索树来说是最坏的情况，而结果却是六个节点的树所能达到的最矮形状。`,"With the repair built into insert and delete, the height stays near log₂ n. A million values: about 20 levels.":`把修复内置到插入和删除中，高度就保持在 log₂ n 附近。一百万个值：大约 20 层。`,"AVL trees and red-black trees work this way. They are behind most sorted maps and sets.":`AVL 树和红黑树就是这样工作的。大多数有序映射和有序集合背后都是它们。`,"Unrepaired, this would be a chain of height 5.":`如果不修复，这会是一条高度为 5 的链。`},tries:t,"segment-trees":{"if range is one cell: node ← that value":`如果 range 只有一个格子: node ← 那个值`,"else: node ← build(left half) + build(right half)":`否则: node ← build(左半) + build(右半)`,"if the node's range is inside range: return node":`如果 节点的范围在 range 之内: 返回 node`,"if it is outside: return 0":`如果 它在范围之外: 返回 0`,"return query(left child) + query(right child)":`返回 query(左孩子) + query(右孩子)`,"change that leaf":`修改那片叶子`,"recompute every node on the way up to the root":`重新计算往上到根的路上的每个节点`,"Range sums that keep changing":`不断变化的区间和`,"Prefix sums answer “what do cells i to j add up to?” instantly. But change one value and every total after it is wrong: an update costs O(n).":`前缀和能立刻回答“格子 i 到 j 加起来是多少？”。但改一个值，它后面的每个累计和就都错了：一次更新要 O(n)。`,"When the data keeps changing, something else is needed. Start with the array itself: 2, 5, 1, 4.":`数据一直在变的时候，就需要别的东西。先从数组本身开始：2、5、1、4。`,"Nodes touched":`触及的节点`,"Sums of pairs, then pairs of pairs":`两两相加，再两两相加`,"Above each pair of cells put their sum: 7 and 5. Above those, their sum: 12.":`在每对格子上方放上它们的和：7 和 5。再在它们上方放上它们的和：12。`,"Every node holds the total of the stretch of the array beneath it. This is a <strong>segment tree</strong>.":`每个节点都存着它下方那一段数组的总和。这就是<strong>线段树</strong>。`,"Built once, in O(n).":`构建一次，O(n)。`,"A query takes whole nodes":`查询使用整个节点`,"What do cells 0 to 2 add up to? Cells 0 and 1 are covered exactly by the node 7, so take it whole. Cell 2 is the leaf 1.":`格子 0 到 2 加起来是多少？格子 0 和 1 正好被节点 7 覆盖，所以整个拿来。格子 2 是叶子 1。`,"7 + 1 = 8, from two nodes instead of three cells. On a big array a query never needs more than about two nodes per level.":`7 + 1 = 8，用了两个节点而不是三个格子。在大数组上，一次查询每层最多只需要两个左右的节点。`,"An update starts at a leaf":`更新从一片叶子开始`,Update:`更新`,"Change cell 1 from 5 to 6. Only one leaf holds that value.":`把格子 1 从 5 改成 6。只有一片叶子存着这个值。`,"was 5":`原来是 5`,"Then fixes the path above it":`然后修正它上方的路径`,"The nodes that include cell 1 are the ones on the way up to the root: 7 becomes 8, and 12 becomes 13.":`包含格子 1 的节点，就是往上到根的路上的那些：7 变成 8，12 变成 13。`,"Nothing else in the tree covers that cell, so nothing else changes.":`树里没有别的节点覆盖这个格子，所以别的都不变。`,"Quick both ways":`两种操作都快`,"A query and an update each touch a handful of nodes per level, and there are about log n levels.":`查询和更新每层都只触及几个节点，而一共大约有 log n 层。`,"Swap the + for “smaller of” or “bigger of” and the same tree answers range minimum or range maximum.":`把 + 换成“较小的”或“较大的”，同一棵树就能回答区间最小值或区间最大值。`,"O(log n) to query and to update. Prefix sums are O(1) and O(n).":`查询和更新都是 O(log n)。前缀和是 O(1) 和 O(n)。`},"binary-heaps":{"put x in the next free place":`把 x 放到下一个空位`,"while x is smaller than its parent:":`当 x 比它的父节点小:`,"swap them                // sift up":`交换它们                // 上浮`,"keep the root to hand back":`留住根，准备交回去`,"move the last item to the root":`把最后一项移到根`,"while it is bigger than a child:":`当 它比某个孩子大:`,"swap it with its smaller child   // sift down":`把它和较小的孩子交换   // 下沉`,"return what was kept":`返回 留住的那个`,"The heap":`堆`,"Smallest on top":`最小的在顶上`,"A <strong>heap</strong> is a binary tree with one rule: every node is smaller than its children. So the smallest value of all is always at the root.":`<strong>堆</strong>是带有一条规则的二叉树：每个节点都比它的孩子小。所以所有值中最小的，总在根上。`,"That is the only promise. 9 is on the left and 8 on the right; a heap is not sorted, and it is not a search tree. It is just enough order to find the minimum instantly.":`这是它唯一的承诺。9 在左边，8 在右边；堆不是有序的，也不是搜索树。它的顺序刚好够立刻找到最小值。`,"Two kinds":`两种`,"This is a min-heap. Turn the rule round, parents bigger than children, and it is a max-heap.":`这是最小堆。把规则反过来，父节点比孩子大，就是最大堆。`,"the smallest":`最小的`,"As an array":`作为数组`,Smallest:`最小`,Items:`项`,"Really an array":`其实是数组`,"A heap is always filled level by level, left to right, with no gaps. Number the nodes in that order and the tree fits in a plain array: no pointers at all.":`堆总是一层一层、从左到右地填满，不留空隙。按这个顺序给节点编号，树就能放进一个普通数组：完全不需要指针。`,"The node at index i has its children at 2i + 1 and 2i + 2, and its parent at (i − 1) ÷ 2, rounded down. Index 1 holds 5; its children are at 3 and 4: 9 and 7.":`下标 i 处节点的孩子在 2i + 1 和 2i + 2，父节点在 (i − 1) ÷ 2，向下取整。下标 1 存着 5；它的孩子在 3 和 4：9 和 7。`,"Read the tree level by level.":`一层一层地读这棵树。`,"Insert at the end":`插在末尾`,"To add 4, put it in the next free place: the end of the array, the next gap in the bottom row.":`要添加 4，就把它放到下一个空位：数组的末尾，也就是最底一行的下一个空隙。`,"The shape is right, but the rule is broken. 4 is smaller than its parent, 8.":`形状是对的，但规则被破坏了。4 比它的父节点 8 小。`,"4 < 8: out of order":`4 < 8：顺序不对`,"Sift up":`上浮`,"Swap 4 with its parent. Now compare again, one level up: 4 is bigger than 3, so it stops there.":`把 4 和它的父节点交换。然后在上一层再比较一次：4 比 3 大，所以停在那里。`,"A new item only ever climbs its own path towards the root. The rest of the heap is never touched.":`新项只会沿着它自己通往根的路径往上爬。堆的其余部分从不被碰到。`,"At most one swap per level: O(log n).":`每层最多交换一次：O(log n)。`,"4 > 3: stop":`4 > 3：停止`,"Take the smallest":`取出最小的`,"The smallest is the root, so taking it is easy. But that leaves a hole at the top.":`最小的就是根，所以取它很容易。但这会在顶上留下一个洞。`,"Fill it with the last item, 8. That keeps the shape complete, and breaks the rule again: 8 is bigger than both its children.":`用最后一项 8 填上它。这样形状保持完整，但规则又被破坏了：8 比它的两个孩子都大。`,"too big for the top":`放在顶上太大了`,"Handed back: 3.":`交回：3。`,"Sift down":`下沉`,"Swap 8 with its <em>smaller</em> child, 4, so that the new parent is smaller than both. Then look again: 8 is smaller than 12, so it stops.":`把 8 和它<em>较小</em>的孩子 4 交换，这样新的父节点比两个孩子都小。然后再看：8 比 12 小，所以停止。`,"The next smallest value is now on top, ready to be taken.":`下一个最小的值现在在顶上，随时可以取走。`,"O(log n) to insert or remove, O(1) to look at the smallest.":`插入或删除 O(log n)，查看最小值 O(1)。`,"8 < 12: stop":`8 < 12：停止`},"building-a-heap":{"for i from the last parent back to the root:":`对于 i 从最后一个父节点倒着到根:`,"sift a[i] down":`让 a[i] 下沉`,"while a[i] is bigger than a child:":`当 a[i] 比某个孩子大:`,"swap it with its smaller child":`把它和较小的孩子交换`,"Any array is a tree":`任何数组都是一棵树`,"Read level by level, any array is a complete binary tree. This one, 9 7 8 3 5 4, is just not a heap yet: parents are bigger than their children all over the place.":`一层一层地读，任何数组都是一棵完全二叉树。这个数组 9 7 8 3 5 4 只是还不是堆：到处都是父节点比孩子大。`,"It could be fixed by inserting the items one at a time, at O(n log n). There is a faster way.":`可以一次插入一项来修好它，代价是 O(n log n)。还有更快的方法。`,"Swaps so far":`已交换次数`,"Start at the last parent":`从最后一个父节点开始`,"The leaves need no work: a node with no children cannot break the rule. So begin with the last node that <em>has</em> a child, 8, and sift it down.":`叶子不需要处理：没有孩子的节点不可能破坏规则。所以从最后一个<em>有</em>孩子的节点 8 开始，让它下沉。`,"8 is bigger than its child 4. Swap them.":`8 比它的孩子 4 大。交换它们。`,"8 > 4: swapped":`8 > 4：已交换`,"Work backwards":`倒着往前做`,"The parent before that is 7. Its children are 3 and 5; swap with the smaller, 3.":`再往前的父节点是 7。它的孩子是 3 和 5；和较小的 3 交换。`,"Each small subtree is made into a heap before the node above it is looked at.":`每棵小子树都先变成堆，然后才去看它上面的节点。`,"7 > 3: swapped":`7 > 3：已交换`,"The root sinks":`根往下沉`,"Last, the root. 9 is bigger than both children, 3 and 4. It swaps with the smaller, 3.":`最后是根。9 比它的两个孩子 3 和 4 都大。它和较小的 3 交换。`,"Both subtrees were already heaps, so this is an ordinary sift-down.":`两棵子树都已经是堆了，所以这只是普通的下沉。`,"still too big":`还是太大`,"As far as it needs to":`需要多远就走多远`,"9 is still bigger than its new children, 7 and 5. Swap with 5, and it reaches the bottom.":`9 还是比它的新孩子 7 和 5 大。和 5 交换，它就到了底部。`,"Every parent is now smaller than its children. It is a heap.":`现在每个父节点都比它的孩子小。这是一个堆了。`,"Cheaper than it looks":`比看起来便宜`,"Four swaps for six items. The reason it is fast: half the nodes are leaves and do nothing, a quarter can sink at most one level, an eighth at most two.":`六个项交换了四次。它快的原因是：一半的节点是叶子，什么都不用做；四分之一最多下沉一层，八分之一最多两层。`,"Only the root can travel the whole height. Added up, the work is proportional to n, not n log n.":`只有根可能走完整个高度。加起来，工作量与 n 成正比，而不是 n log n。`,"O(n) to build a heap from an array. Heap sort begins with exactly this.":`从数组建堆是 O(n)。堆排序就是从这一步开始的。`},"priority-queues":{"insert it into the heap":`把它插入堆中`,"take the smallest from the heap":`从堆中取出最小的`,"return the root, leaving it there":`返回 根，并把它留在原处`,"Who goes next":`下一个是谁`,"Most urgent first":`最紧急的优先`,"An ordinary queue serves whoever has waited longest. A hospital does not work like that: the most urgent case is seen first, whenever it arrived.":`普通队列服务的是等得最久的人。医院不是这样运作的：最紧急的病人先看，不管他什么时候来的。`,"A <strong>priority queue</strong> does the same. Every item has a priority, and the one that comes out is always the most urgent: here, the smallest number.":`<strong>优先队列</strong>也是这样。每个项都有一个优先级，出来的总是最紧急的那个：这里是数字最小的。`,"How it is built":`它是怎么实现的`,"A priority queue says what it does. A heap is the usual way of doing it.":`优先队列说的是它做什么。堆是实现它的常用方法。`,"next to be served":`下一个被服务`,Served:`已服务`,"Waiting is listed in the order they arrived.":`等待中的按到达顺序列出。`,"Push: a routine case":`push：一个普通病例`,"A patient with priority 6 arrives. Less urgent than everyone already waiting, so after one comparison with its parent it stays at the bottom.":`一个优先级为 6 的病人到了。比所有在等的人都不紧急，所以和父节点比较一次后，它留在底部。`,"Nothing else moved.":`其他什么都没动。`,"Push: an emergency":`push：一个急诊`,"Now a priority 1 arrives, last of all. It starts at the bottom like anyone else, but it is more urgent than its parent, 5, so they swap.":`现在一个优先级为 1 的病人最后到达。它像其他人一样从底部开始，但它比父节点 5 更紧急，所以两者交换。`,"1 < 5: move up":`1 < 5：上移`,"Straight to the front":`直接到最前面`,"And it is more urgent than 3, so they swap too. Two swaps, and the last to arrive is the next to be served.":`它也比 3 更紧急，所以也交换。两次交换，最后到达的成了下一个被服务的。`,"It did not push past everyone. It only compared itself with the two nodes on its own path to the root.":`它并没有挤过所有人。它只和自己通往根的路径上的两个节点比较过。`,"O(log n): one comparison per level, however many are waiting.":`O(log n)：每层一次比较，不管有多少人在等。`,"<strong>pop()</strong> takes the root: priority 1 is served. The last item, 5, fills the gap and sifts down past 3.":`<strong>pop()</strong> 取走根：优先级 1 被服务。最后一项 5 填上空位，下沉越过 3。`,"The heap has put the next most urgent case on top by itself. That is 3, which arrived before nearly everyone.":`堆自己把下一个最紧急的病例放到了顶上。那是 3，它几乎比所有人来得都早。`,"Why a heap":`为什么用堆`,"You could keep the waiting list unsorted: adding is instant, but finding the most urgent means checking everyone. Or keep it sorted: the most urgent is at the front, but every arrival has to be slotted in.":`你可以让等待列表保持无序：添加是即时的，但找最紧急的要检查每个人。或者让它保持有序：最紧急的在最前面，但每次有人到达都得插到正确的位置。`,"A heap is quick at both, because it keeps only as much order as the job needs.":`堆两样都快，因为它只保持这项工作所需的那么多顺序。`,"Operating-system schedulers, event simulations, and the shortest-path search later in this course.":`操作系统调度器、事件模拟，以及本课程后面的最短路径搜索。`,"Unsorted list":`无序列表`,"Sorted list":`有序列表`,Heap:`堆`,"Both jobs matter, so the heap wins.":`两样工作都重要，所以堆胜出。`},"top-k":{"heap ← an empty min-heap":`heap ← 一个空的最小堆`,"for each x in the stream:":`对每个 流中的 x:`,"if the heap holds fewer than k: insert x":`如果 堆中少于 k 个: 插入 x`,"else if x > the heap's smallest:":`否则，如果 x > 堆中最小的:`,"take the smallest out, insert x":`取出最小的，插入 x`,"// otherwise x is not in the top k: drop it":`// 否则 x 不在前 k 名里：丢掉它`,"return what the heap holds":`返回 堆中存的东西`,"So far":`目前为止`,"The three biggest":`最大的三个`,"Numbers arrive one at a time: 5, 9, 2, 7, 1, 8… Keep track of the <strong>three biggest</strong> seen so far.":`数字一个一个地到来：5、9、2、7、1、8……记住目前见过的<strong>最大的三个</strong>。`,"Sorting everything works, but it does far too much, and a stream may never end. The trick is to remember only three numbers, in a heap.":`全部排序也行，但做得太多了，而且一个流可能永远不会结束。诀窍是只记住三个数，放在一个堆里。`,"first to arrive":`最先到达`,Stream:`流`,"Top 3 so far":`目前的前 3 名`,"Smallest of them":`它们中最小的`,"Fill the heap":`填满堆`,"The first three go straight in. It is a <strong>min</strong>-heap, so the smallest of the three, 2, sits on top.":`前三个直接放进去。这是一个<strong>最小</strong>堆，所以三个中最小的 2 在顶上。`,"That seems backwards for finding the biggest. But the one on top is the one most at risk: the weakest of the current top three.":`要找最大的，这看起来是反的。但顶上的那个正是最危险的：当前前三名里最弱的。`,"To stay in the top three, a newcomer only has to beat the weakest member.":`新来的只要胜过最弱的成员，就能留在前三名里。`,"weakest of the three":`三个中最弱的`,"A newcomer":`新来的`,"7 arrives. Compare it with the root, and only the root: 7 is bigger than 2.":`7 来了。把它和根比较，只和根比较：7 比 2 大。`,"So 7 belongs in the top three, and 2 no longer does.":`所以 7 属于前三名，而 2 不再属于。`,"7 > 2: it is in":`7 > 2：入选`,Replace:`替换`,"2 is taken out and 7 inserted. The heap sorts itself out, and the new weakest member, 5, rises to the top.":`取出 2，插入 7。堆自己整理好，新的最弱成员 5 升到顶上。`,"The heap never grows past three items, however long the stream is.":`不管流有多长，堆都不会超过三个项。`,"Not good enough":`不够好`,"1 arrives. It is smaller than the root, 5, so it is smaller than all three of them.":`1 来了。它比根 5 小，所以比三个都小。`,"One comparison and it is gone. Most of a stream is dismissed this cheaply.":`一次比较，它就被淘汰了。流中的大部分数都是这样便宜地被打发掉的。`,"1 < 5: dropped":`1 < 5：丢掉`,"The answer so far":`目前的答案`,"8 beats 5, so 5 goes and 8 comes in. The heap now holds 9, 8 and 7: the three biggest of everything seen.":`8 胜过 5，所以 5 出去，8 进来。现在堆中是 9、8 和 7：目前见过的所有数中最大的三个。`,"Stop the stream at any moment and the answer is ready.":`随时停下这个流，答案都是现成的。`,"O(n log k) time and only O(k) memory, where sorting needs O(n log n) and all n items.":`O(n log k) 时间，只要 O(k) 内存，而排序需要 O(n log n) 并且要存下全部 n 个项。`,"third biggest":`第三大`,"Six numbers seen, three remembered.":`见过六个数，记住了三个。`},"median-of-a-stream":{"if x is no bigger than the top of low: push it on low":`如果 x 不大于 low 的顶部: 把它压入 low`,"else: push it on high":`否则: 把它压入 high`,"if one heap has two more than the other:":`如果 一个堆比另一个多两个:`,"move its top across":`把它的顶部移过去`,"if the heaps are the same size:":`如果 两个堆一样大:`,"return the average of their two tops":`返回 它们两个顶部的平均值`,"return the top of the bigger heap":`返回 较大的堆的顶部`,"The two halves":`两半`,"The middle of a moving list":`一个不断变化的列表的中间`,"Numbers arrive one at a time, and after each you may be asked for the <strong>median</strong>: the middle value. Sorting after every arrival is far too slow.":`数字一个一个地到来，每来一个，你都可能被问到<strong>中位数</strong>：中间的值。每来一个就排一次序太慢了。`,"The trick is that the median only depends on the numbers either side of the middle. So keep the numbers in two halves, and watch where they meet.":`诀窍在于中位数只取决于中间两侧的数。所以把数分成两半存放，看它们在哪里相接。`,"Lower half":`下半部分`,"biggest on top":`最大的在顶上`,"Upper half":`上半部分`,"smallest on top":`最小的在顶上`,Median:`中位数`,"A heap each side":`每边一个堆`,"After 5 and 2: the smaller goes on the left, the bigger on the right. The left side is a <em>max</em>-heap, so its biggest is on top. The right is a <em>min</em>-heap, with its smallest on top.":`5 和 2 之后：小的放左边，大的放右边。左边是<em>最大</em>堆，所以它最大的在顶上。右边是<em>最小</em>堆，最小的在顶上。`,"Those two tops are the numbers nearest the middle. With one each, the median is halfway between: 3.5.":`这两个顶部就是最接近中间的数。每边一个时，中位数在它们正中间：3.5。`,"median 3.5":`中位数 3.5`,"Which side does it belong to?":`它属于哪一边？`,"8 arrives. It is bigger than the top of the lower half, so it goes on the right, and sinks below 5.":`8 来了。它比下半部分的顶部大，所以放到右边，沉到 5 下面。`,"The right side now has one more. The median is the top of the bigger side: 5.":`右边现在多一个。中位数就是较大那一边的顶部：5。`,"median 5":`中位数 5`,"Even again":`又一样多了`,"1 arrives and belongs on the left, under 2. Two each: the median is the average of the tops again, 3.5.":`1 来了，属于左边，在 2 下面。每边两个：中位数又是两个顶部的平均值，3.5。`,Lopsided:`一边倒`,"9 and then 7 both belong on the right. That would leave four on the right against two on the left: the halves are no longer halves.":`9 和 7 都属于右边。那样右边就有四个，左边只有两个：两半不再是两半了。`,"7 is still to come.":`7 还没来。`,"Pass one across":`移一个过去`,Rebalance:`再平衡`,"So when 7 goes in on the right, the right’s top, 5, moves over to the left. It is the smallest of the upper half, which makes it the biggest of the lower.":`所以当 7 放进右边时，右边的顶部 5 移到左边。它是上半部分中最小的，所以它就成了下半部分中最大的。`,"Three each. The tops are 5 and 7, and the median is 6.":`每边三个。顶部是 5 和 7，中位数是 6。`,"O(log n) to add a number, O(1) to read the median.":`添加一个数 O(log n)，读取中位数 O(1)。`,"median 6":`中位数 6`},"heap-sort":{"arrange a as a max-heap":`把 a 整理成一个最大堆`,"for end from the last cell down to the second:":`对于 end 从最后一个格子倒着到第二个:`,"swap a[0] with a[end]      // the biggest goes to the end":`交换 a[0] 和 a[end]      // 最大的去末尾`,"sift a[0] down, ignoring cells from end onwards":`让 a[0] 下沉，忽略从 end 开始的格子`,"In the array":`在数组中`,"A heap knows its biggest":`堆知道它最大的是谁`,"This is a <strong>max-heap</strong>: every parent is bigger than its children, so the biggest value is at the root.":`这是一个<strong>最大堆</strong>：每个父节点都比它的孩子大，所以最大的值在根上。`,"Sorting with it is simple to state. Take the biggest, then the biggest of what is left, and so on. The clever part is where the taken values are kept.":`用它排序，说起来很简单。取出最大的，再取出剩下的里面最大的，依此类推。巧妙之处在于取出的值存放在哪里。`,"the biggest":`最大的`,"Still a heap":`仍是堆`,Sorted:`已排序`,"Swap it to the end":`把它换到末尾`,"Swap the root with the last item of the heap. 9 is now in the last cell of the array, which is exactly where the biggest value belongs.":`把根和堆的最后一项交换。9 现在在数组的最后一个格子里，正是最大的值该在的地方。`,"Fence that cell off. The heap is one smaller, and its root is wrong.":`把那个格子隔开。堆少了一个，而它的根不对了。`,"Repair the heap":`修复堆`,"Sift the new root down, as when taking from any heap: 4 swaps with its bigger child, 8. The fenced cell is not looked at.":`让新的根下沉，和从任何堆中取值时一样：4 和它较大的孩子 8 交换。隔开的格子不看。`,"The biggest of what remains is on top again.":`剩下的里面最大的又在顶上了。`,"Swap 8 to the end of the heap, beside 9, and fence it off. Sift 5 down past 7.":`把 8 换到堆的末尾，在 9 旁边，把它隔开。让 5 下沉越过 7。`,"The sorted part grows from the back of the array as the heap shrinks from the front.":`随着堆从前面缩小，已排序的部分从数组后面增长。`,"7 goes to the end of the heap and is fenced off. 3, now on top, sifts down past 5.":`7 去到堆的末尾并被隔开。现在在顶上的 3 下沉越过 5。`,"Half the array is sorted, and the heap is down to three.":`数组排好了一半，堆只剩三个。`,"Until the heap is gone":`直到堆没了`,"Two more rounds and nothing is left in the heap. Read the tree level by level, which is the order of the array: 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9.":`再来两轮，堆里就什么都不剩了。一层一层地读这棵树，也就是数组的顺序：3、4、5、7、8、9。`,"No second array was needed. The heap and the sorted part shared the one array throughout.":`不需要第二个数组。堆和已排序的部分始终共用同一个数组。`,"O(n log n) always, with O(1) extra memory. It does not keep equal items in their original order.":`总是 O(n log n)，额外内存 O(1)。它不会让相等的项保持原来的顺序。`},"graph-representation":{"How it is stored":`它是怎么存储的`,"Things…":`一些东西……`,"A list puts things in a line. A tree puts them in a hierarchy. Most of the world is neither: towns joined by roads, people who know each other, pages that link to pages.":`列表把东西排成一行。树把它们排成层级。世界上大多数东西两者都不是：用道路相连的城镇、互相认识的人、互相链接的网页。`,"A <strong>graph</strong> is how to hold that. It starts with a set of things, called <strong>nodes</strong> (or vertices).":`<strong>图</strong>就是用来存放这些的。它从一组东西开始，这些东西叫<strong>节点</strong>（或顶点）。`,"no neighbours":`没有邻居`,"Six nodes, nothing joining them yet.":`六个节点，还没有任何连接。`,"…and the links between them":`……以及它们之间的连接`,"Then come the <strong>edges</strong>: each one joins two nodes. That is all a graph is. There is no first node, no root, no order.":`然后是<strong>边</strong>：每条边连接两个节点。图就是这么简单。没有第一个节点，没有根，也没有顺序。`,"A linked list is a graph where every node has one way on. A tree is a graph with no loops. Graphs are the general case.":`链表是每个节点只有一条出路的图。树是没有环的图。图是一般情况。`,"Each row lists a node’s neighbours.":`每一行列出一个节点的邻居。`,"Two nodes joined by an edge are <strong>neighbours</strong>. B has three: A, D and E.":`由一条边相连的两个节点互为<strong>邻居</strong>。B 有三个：A、D 和 E。`,"Nearly every graph algorithm comes down to one move, repeated: “for each neighbour of this node…”. So the way a graph is stored has to make that move quick.":`几乎每个图算法都归结为一个反复进行的动作：“对这个节点的每个邻居……”。所以图的存储方式必须让这个动作很快。`,"An adjacency list":`邻接表`,"The usual way: for every node, keep a list of its neighbours. To visit E’s neighbours, go to E’s list and read it: B, F.":`常用的方法：为每个节点保存一个邻居列表。要访问 E 的邻居，就去 E 的列表读：B、F。`,"It takes space for each node and each edge and nothing more. For graphs where most pairs are <em>not</em> joined, which is almost all real ones, this is what you want.":`它只为每个节点和每条边占用空间，别无其他。对于大多数节点对<em>没有</em>相连的图，也就是几乎所有真实的图，这正是你想要的。`,"Space O(V + E). Listing a node’s neighbours takes as long as it has neighbours.":`空间 O(V + E)。列出一个节点的邻居，所需时间和它的邻居数一样多。`,"An adjacency matrix":`邻接矩阵`,"The other way: a grid with a row and a column for every node, and a 1 wherever two are joined. “Is C joined to F?” is one look: row C, column F.":`另一种方法：一个网格，每个节点占一行一列，两个节点相连的地方写 1。“C 和 F 相连吗？”看一眼就知道：C 行，F 列。`,"That answer is instant. But the grid has a cell for every possible pair, used or not, and finding a node’s neighbours means reading its whole row.":`这个答案是即时的。但网格为每一对可能的节点都留了一个格子，不管用没用到，而且找一个节点的邻居要读完它整行。`,"Space O(V²). Good for small or dense graphs; wasteful for big sparse ones.":`空间 O(V²)。适合小的或稠密的图；对大的稀疏图很浪费。`,"Columns run A to F, like the rows.":`列和行一样，从 A 到 F。`,"Direction and weight":`方向与权重`,Variations:`变体`,"Two things can be added to an edge. A <strong>weight</strong>: a number for what it costs to use, such as a distance or a time. And a <strong>direction</strong>: a one-way street, or “follows” on a social network.":`一条边可以多加两样东西。<strong>权重</strong>：表示使用它的代价的数字，比如距离或时间。还有<strong>方向</strong>：一条单行道，或者社交网络上的“关注”。`,"Either store is easily extended. A list keeps the weight beside each neighbour; a matrix puts the weight where the 1 was.":`两种存储方式都很容易扩展。邻接表在每个邻居旁边存上权重；邻接矩阵把权重写在原来写 1 的地方。`,"Each neighbour, with the weight of the edge to it.":`每个邻居，以及通往它的边的权重。`},"breadth-first-search":{"mark start as seen, put it in a queue":`把 start 标记为已见，放进一个队列`,"node ← take the front of the queue":`node ← 取出队首`,"mark it as seen":`把它标记为已见`,"put it at the back of the queue":`把它放到队尾`,"Waiting their turn":`等着轮到它们`,"Nearest first":`最近的优先`,"Starting from A, visit every node that can be reached. A graph has no order of its own, so the search has to choose one.":`从 A 出发，访问所有能到达的节点。图本身没有顺序，所以搜索必须自己选一个。`,"<strong>Breadth-first search</strong> goes outwards in rings: everything one edge away, then everything two away, and so on. It is how a ripple spreads.":`<strong>广度优先搜索</strong>一圈一圈地向外扩展：先是一条边之外的一切，然后是两条边之外的一切，依此类推。就像涟漪扩散那样。`,Queue:`队列`,"The first ring":`第一圈`,"A is at distance 0. Look at each of its neighbours: B and C have not been seen, so mark them and put them in a <strong>queue</strong>.":`A 的距离是 0。看它的每个邻居：B 和 C 还没见过，所以标记它们，并放进一个<strong>队列</strong>。`,"The number on a node is how many edges it is from A.":`节点上的数字是它离 A 有几条边。`,"The queue keeps the order":`队列保持顺序`,"B is at the front, so B goes next. Its unseen neighbours, D and E, are two edges from A. They join the <em>back</em> of the queue, behind C.":`B 在队首，所以下一个是 B。它没见过的邻居 D 和 E，离 A 有两条边。它们排到队列的<em>末尾</em>，在 C 后面。`,"Because it is a queue, everything at distance 1 is dealt with before anything at distance 2.":`因为这是队列，所有距离为 1 的都会在距离为 2 的之前处理完。`,"Seen means skip":`见过就跳过`,"C’s turn. One neighbour, A, is already seen, so it is skipped. The other, F, is new.":`轮到 C。一个邻居 A 已经见过，所以跳过。另一个 F 是新的。`,"Marking nodes as seen is what stops the search going round in circles, and what makes sure each node is handled once.":`把节点标记为已见，才让搜索不会绕圈子，并且保证每个节点只处理一次。`,"Fewest edges":`边数最少`,"D, E and F have no unseen neighbours, so the queue empties and the search is over. The edge between E and F was never needed.":`D、E 和 F 都没有没见过的邻居，所以队列清空，搜索结束。E 和 F 之间的边根本没用上。`,"Every node now carries its distance from A, and the coloured edges are the shortest routes. In a graph without weights, breadth-first search <em>is</em> the shortest-path algorithm.":`现在每个节点都带着它离 A 的距离，着色的边就是最短的路线。在没有权重的图里，广度优先搜索<em>就是</em>最短路径算法。`,"O(V + E): each node enters the queue once, and each edge is looked at twice.":`O(V + E)：每个节点进队列一次，每条边看两次。`,"2 edges from A":`离 A 两条边`,"Visited in order of distance.":`按距离顺序访问。`},"depth-first-search":{"mark node as seen":`把 node 标记为已见`,"dfs(neighbour)        // go deeper":`dfs(neighbour)        // 走得更深`,"// nothing left here: go back":`// 这里什么都不剩了：往回走`,"Where it has been":`它走过的地方`,"As far as it goes":`能走多远走多远`,"Breadth-first search spreads out evenly. <strong>Depth-first search</strong> does the opposite: pick a way and follow it as far as it goes, and only come back when there is nowhere new to go.":`广度优先搜索均匀地铺开。<strong>深度优先搜索</strong>正好相反：选一条路一直走到底，只有在没有新地方可去时才回来。`,"It is how you would explore a maze with a ball of string.":`就像你拿着一团线去探索迷宫。`,"Path from the start":`从起点出发的路径`,"the stack":`栈`,"Go deep":`往深处走`,"From A take the first unseen neighbour, B. Do not look at A’s other neighbour yet. From B take its first unseen neighbour, D.":`从 A 走向第一个没见过的邻居 B。先不看 A 的另一个邻居。从 B 走向它第一个没见过的邻居 D。`,"The numbers are the order nodes were first reached in.":`数字是各节点第一次被到达的顺序。`,"Dead end: back up":`死路：退回`,"D has no unseen neighbours, so it is finished. Go <strong>back</strong> the way you came, to B, and try B’s next neighbour: E.":`D 没有没见过的邻居，所以它完成了。沿着来路<strong>退回</strong> B，试试 B 的下一个邻居：E。`,"Going back is the string being wound in. In code it is a function returning, or a stack being popped.":`往回走就是收线。在代码里，就是函数返回，或者栈弹出。`,"Deep again":`再往深处走`,"From E on to F, and from F on to C. Each time the search just takes the next step it can.":`从 E 到 F，再从 F 到 C。每次搜索都只是走它能走的下一步。`,"Notice C: it is right next to A, and it is the last node reached.":`注意 C：它就在 A 旁边，却是最后到达的节点。`,Unwind:`回退`,"C’s only other neighbour is A, already seen. So back to F, to E, to B, to A, each with nothing new to offer.":`C 唯一的另一个邻居是 A，已经见过了。所以退回 F、E、B、A，每一个都没有新东西了。`,"Back at the start with nothing left: every node has been visited once.":`回到起点，什么都不剩：每个节点都被访问了一次。`,"O(V + E), the same as breadth-first. Only the order differs.":`O(V + E)，和广度优先一样。只是顺序不同。`,"Finished deepest first.":`最深的最先完成。`,"A way, not the best way":`一条路，而不是最好的路`,"Depth-first search reached C through B, E and F: four edges, when C is one edge from A. It finds <em>a</em> route, not the shortest one.":`深度优先搜索经过 B、E 和 F 才到达 C：四条边，而 C 离 A 只有一条边。它找到的是<em>一条</em>路线，而不是最短的那条。`,"What it is good at is questions about structure: is there any way through, is there a loop, what has to come before what. And it needs only a stack, which recursion gives for free.":`它擅长的是关于结构的问题：有没有路能通过、有没有环、什么必须在什么之前。而且它只需要一个栈，递归免费就提供了。`,"Nearest or fewest steps: breadth-first. Everything, in some order, or anything about loops: depth-first.":`最近的或步数最少：广度优先。全部访问一遍，或者任何关于环的问题：深度优先。`,"4 edges, not 1":`4 条边，而不是 1 条`},"connected-components":{"for each node:":`对每个 节点:`,"if it has no label yet:":`如果 它还没有标签:`,"spread out from it, labelling":`从它向外扩展，把`,"everything reached with count":`到达的一切都标记为 count`,"The pieces":`各个部分`,"How many pieces?":`有几个部分？`,"A graph need not be all in one piece. This one clearly is not, but a program cannot see that at a glance: it has only a list of edges.":`图不一定是连成一整块的。这个图显然不是，但程序没法一眼看出来：它只有一张边的列表。`,"Each piece, in which every node can reach every other, is a <strong>connected component</strong>.":`每个部分中，每个节点都能到达其他所有节点，这样的部分叫作<strong>连通分量</strong>。`,"Groups found":`已找到的组`,"Spread from any node":`从任意节点扩展`,"Pick a node that has no label, A, and search outwards from it: breadth-first or depth-first, either will do. Everything reached gets the label 1.":`选一个没有标签的节点 A，从它向外搜索：广度优先或深度优先都行。到达的一切都得到标签 1。`,"The search stops by itself when the piece runs out.":`这个部分走完时，搜索会自己停下。`,"Find the next unlabelled one":`找下一个没有标签的`,"Carry on down the list of nodes. B and C are already labelled, so skip them. D is not: it starts piece 2, and the search from it finds E.":`沿着节点列表继续往下。B 和 C 已经有标签了，跳过。D 没有：它开始第 2 部分，从它出发的搜索找到了 E。`,"A piece of one":`只有一个的部分`,"F has no label and no edges. It is a component all by itself: piece 3.":`F 没有标签，也没有边。它自己就是一个连通分量：第 3 部分。`,"on its own":`独自一个`,"The paint bucket":`油漆桶`,"Three pieces. Every node was labelled once and every edge looked at twice.":`三个部分。每个节点被标记一次，每条边被看两次。`,"On a grid, where a cell’s neighbours are the cells beside it, this is <strong>flood fill</strong>: the paint-bucket tool, counting islands on a map, finding the rooms in a floor plan.":`在网格上，一个格子的邻居就是它旁边的格子，这就是<strong>泛洪填充</strong>：油漆桶工具、数地图上的岛屿、找出平面图里的房间。`,"O(V + E). Union-find answers the same question when edges arrive one at a time.":`O(V + E)。当边一条一条地到来时，并查集回答的是同一个问题。`},"cycle-detection":{"put node on the path":`把 node 放到路径上`,"for each arrow node → next:":`对每个 箭头 node → next:`,"if next is on the path: return yes":`如果 next 在路径上: 返回 是`,"if next is new and has_cycle(next): return yes":`如果 next 是新的且 has_cycle(next): 返回 是`,"take node off the path, mark it finished":`把 node 从路径上拿下，标记为已完成`,"Going round in circles":`绕圈子`,"If job B waits for D, D waits for C, and C waits for B, none of them can ever start. A loop like that is a <strong>cycle</strong>.":`如果任务 B 等 D，D 等 C，而 C 又等 B，它们谁都永远开始不了。这样的循环叫作<strong>环</strong>。`,"A build system has to refuse it, a spreadsheet has to report a circular reference, and a topological sort has no answer. So: does this graph have one?":`构建系统必须拒绝它，电子表格必须报告循环引用，拓扑排序也没有答案。所以：这个图里有环吗？`,"On the path":`在路径上`,Cycle:`环`,"Remember the way you came":`记住你来的路`,"Search depth-first from A, and keep a note of the <strong>path</strong>: the nodes between the start and where you are standing now.":`从 A 开始深度优先搜索，并记下<strong>路径</strong>：起点和你现在所站位置之间的节点。`,"A, then B, then C. All three are on the path.":`A，然后 B，然后 C。三个都在路径上。`,"A dead end is fine":`死路没关系`,"From C, try E. It has no arrows out, so there is nothing more to find beyond it. Mark it finished and step back to C.":`从 C 试试 E。它没有出去的箭头，所以在它后面再也找不到什么了。把它标记为已完成，退回 C。`,"E comes off the path. A finished node can never be part of a loop through where you are now.":`E 从路径上拿下。一个已完成的节点永远不可能是经过你当前位置的环的一部分。`,finished:`已完成`,"An arrow back onto the path":`一个指回路径上的箭头`,"C’s other arrow goes to D, and D’s arrow goes to B. But B is <em>on the path</em>: it is one of the nodes that led here.":`C 的另一个箭头指向 D，而 D 的箭头指向 B。但 B <em>在路径上</em>：它是通向这里的节点之一。`,"So there is a way from B to D, and now an arrow from D back to B. That is a cycle: B, C, D, and round again.":`所以从 B 有路到 D，现在又有一个从 D 指回 B 的箭头。这就是一个环：B、C、D，再绕回来。`,"already on the path":`已经在路径上`,"Visited is not enough":`只看“访问过”还不够`,"The rule needs three kinds of node: new, on the path, and finished. Meeting a finished node again is harmless: two routes to the same place, like a diamond. Only an arrow to a node still on the path closes a loop.":`这条规则需要三种节点：新的、在路径上的、已完成的。再次遇到已完成的节点是无害的：两条路通向同一个地方，就像菱形那样。只有指向仍在路径上的节点的箭头，才会闭合成环。`,"With no arrows, just plain edges, it is simpler: any visited node other than the one you just came from means a cycle.":`如果没有箭头，只有普通的边，就更简单了：除了你刚刚来的那个节点，遇到任何访问过的节点都意味着有环。`,"O(V + E): one depth-first search.":`O(V + E)：一次深度优先搜索。`},"topological-sort":{"count the arrows coming in to each node":`数出指向每个节点的箭头数`,"ready ← every node with none":`ready ← 所有没有箭头指向的节点`,"while ready is not empty:":`当 ready 不为空:`,"take a node from ready, add it to the order":`从 ready 中取出一个节点，把它加到顺序里`,"for each node it points at:":`对每个 它指向的节点:`,"one fewer arrow comes in to that node":`指向那个节点的箭头少一个`,"if none are left: add it to ready":`如果 一个都不剩了: 把它加进 ready`,"if any node was never taken: there is a loop":`如果 有节点从没被取出: 就存在一个环`,"The order":`顺序`,"What must come first":`什么必须先做`,"Six jobs, and some depend on others: an arrow from A to C means A has to be finished before C can start. Courses with prerequisites, steps in a build, getting dressed.":`六项任务，有些依赖于别的：从 A 指向 C 的箭头表示 A 必须完成后 C 才能开始。有先修要求的课程、构建中的步骤、穿衣服。`,"A <strong>topological order</strong> is a way to line the jobs up so that every arrow points forwards. No job comes before something it depends on.":`<strong>拓扑顺序</strong>是一种排列任务的方式，让每个箭头都指向前方。没有任务会排在它所依赖的东西之前。`,"Order so far":`目前的顺序`,"Ready now":`现在可以做`,"Count what each waits for":`数一数每个在等什么`,"For every job, count the arrows coming <em>in</em>: how many things it is still waiting for.":`对每项任务，数出指<em>向</em>它的箭头：它还在等几件事。`,"A and B are waiting for nothing. They can be done right away.":`A 和 B 什么都不等。它们马上就可以做。`,"Do one that is ready":`做一个准备好的`,"Do A. Everything A pointed at now has one thing fewer to wait for: C drops from 2 to 1.":`做 A。A 指向的一切现在都少等一件事：C 从 2 降到 1。`,"C is still waiting for B, so it is not ready yet.":`C 还在等 B，所以它还没准备好。`,"Finishing frees others":`完成一项会释放别的`,"Do B. Its arrows go to C and D, and both drop to zero.":`做 B。它的箭头指向 C 和 D，两个都降到了零。`,"Two more jobs have just become ready. Nothing was searched for: finishing B is what revealed them.":`又有两项任务刚刚准备好。没有搜索任何东西：是完成 B 让它们显现出来的。`,"Keep going":`继续`,"Do C, which frees E. Do D, which leaves F waiting for one thing. Do E, and F is free.":`做 C，它释放了 E。做 D，F 还剩一件事要等。做 E，F 就自由了。`,"Whenever more than one job is ready, either may go first. There is usually more than one valid order.":`每当有不止一项任务准备好时，哪个先做都行。有效的顺序通常不止一种。`,"Every arrow points forwards":`每个箭头都指向前方`,"F is last. The order is A, B, C, D, E, F, and every dependency is respected.":`F 最后。顺序是 A、B、C、D、E、F，每个依赖关系都被遵守了。`,"If jobs were left over with nothing ready, they would be waiting on each other in a circle: a loop, and no order exists. So this is also how dependency loops are detected.":`如果还剩下任务，却没有一个准备好，它们就是在互相绕圈等待：一个环，不存在任何顺序。所以这也是检测依赖环的方法。`,"O(V + E): every job is taken once and every arrow is counted off once.":`O(V + E)：每项任务取出一次，每个箭头扣减一次。`,"Only works on a graph with no loops.":`只适用于没有环的图。`},"strongly-connected-components":{"order ← the nodes, as a depth-first search":`order ← 按深度优先搜索完成的顺序`,"finishes with them":`排列的节点`,"for each node, last finished first:":`对每个 节点，最后完成的优先:`,"if it has no group yet:":`如果 它还没有组:`,"walk the arrows backwards from it,":`从它出发逆着箭头走，`,"labelling every unlabelled node reached":`把到达的每个未标记节点都标记上`,"There, but not back":`能去，但回不来`,"With arrows, getting somewhere and getting back are different questions. From A you can reach F. From F you cannot reach anything.":`有了箭头，到达某处和回来就是不同的问题了。从 A 你能到达 F。从 F 你哪里都到不了。`,"Two nodes are <strong>strongly connected</strong> when each can reach the other. The question is how the graph falls apart into groups like that.":`当两个节点能互相到达时，它们就是<strong>强连通</strong>的。问题是图如何分裂成这样的组。`,"Finished in this order":`按这个顺序完成`,"A loop holds a group together":`环把一组连在一起`,"A points to B, B to C, and C back to A. Start at any of the three and you can get to the other two, and home again.":`A 指向 B，B 指向 C，C 又指回 A。从三个中的任何一个出发，你都能到达另外两个，再回家。`,"These three form one <strong>strongly connected component</strong>.":`这三个构成一个<strong>强连通分量</strong>。`,"A one-way road divides":`一条单行道把它们分开`,"C has a road to D, but nothing comes back from D’s side. So D is not in the first group.":`C 有一条路通向 D，但从 D 那边没有路回来。所以 D 不在第一组里。`,"D and E point at each other: a group of two. F can be reached but leads nowhere: a group of one. Three components, joined by one-way roads.":`D 和 E 互相指向：一个两个节点的组。F 能被到达，但哪里都去不了：一个只有一个节点的组。三个分量，由单行道连接。`,"no way back to C":`没有回 C 的路`,"Pass one: go as deep as you can":`第一遍：尽可能往深处走`,"That was by eye. A program does it with two depth-first searches. The first is an ordinary one: from A, follow arrows as far as they go.":`刚才是用眼睛看的。程序用两次深度优先搜索来做。第一次是普通的：从 A 出发，沿着箭头能走多远走多远。`,"A, B, C, D, E, F. At F there is nowhere left to go.":`A、B、C、D、E、F。到了 F 就无处可去了。`,"Number them on the way out":`在出来的路上编号`,"The search backs out the way it came. Number each node as it is <em>finished</em>: F first, then E, D, C, B, and A last.":`搜索沿着来路退出。在每个节点<em>完成</em>时给它编号：F 最先，然后是 E、D、C、B，A 最后。`,"The node finished last is always in a group that no other group leads into. That is the fact the second pass relies on.":`最后完成的节点，总是在一个没有其他组通向它的组里。第二遍依靠的就是这个事实。`,"Pass two: walk the arrows backwards":`第二遍：逆着箭头走`,"Take the highest number, A, and walk <em>against</em> the arrows. That reaches C, then B. Nothing outside leads into this group, so the walk cannot leak out of it: group 1.":`取编号最大的 A，<em>逆着</em>箭头走。这会到达 C，然后是 B。外面没有东西通向这个组，所以这次行走不会漏出去：第 1 组。`,"The highest number left is D. Backwards from D reaches E, and C is already taken: group 2. Then F by itself: group 3.":`剩下编号最大的是 D。从 D 逆着走到达 E，而 C 已经被占了：第 2 组。然后 F 自己：第 3 组。`,"A map of the groups":`组的地图`,"Shrink each group to a single dot and what is left has no loops at all: group 1 leads to group 2, which leads to group 3. That can be put in topological order.":`把每个组缩成一个点，剩下的部分完全没有环：第 1 组通向第 2 组，第 2 组通向第 3 组。这可以排成拓扑顺序。`,"This is how a build tool finds modules that depend on each other in a circle, and how a compiler finds functions that call each other.":`构建工具就是这样找出互相循环依赖的模块的，编译器也是这样找出互相调用的函数的。`,"O(V + E): two depth-first searches. This two-pass method is Kosaraju’s algorithm.":`O(V + E)：两次深度优先搜索。这种两遍的方法叫 Kosaraju 算法。`},"shortest-paths":{"while some node is not settled:":`当 还有节点没有确定:`,"node ← the nearest unsettled node":`node ← 最近的未确定节点`,"settle it":`确定它`,"for each neighbour, by an edge w:":`对每个 邻居，经过一条权重为 w 的边:`,"if best[node] + w < best[neighbour]:":`如果 best[node] + w < best[neighbour]:`,"Not all edges are equal":`不是所有边都一样`,"When edges have weights, the fewest edges is no longer the shortest way. A to B direct costs 4. A to C to B is two edges, and costs 3.":`边有权重时，边数最少就不再是最短的路了。从 A 直达 B 花费 4。A 经 C 到 B 是两条边，花费 3。`,"<strong>Dijkstra’s algorithm</strong> finds the cheapest route from one node to every other. It is breadth-first search that pays attention to cost.":`<strong>Dijkstra 算法</strong>找出从一个节点到其他每个节点的最便宜路线。它就是关注代价的广度优先搜索。`,"Best guesses":`最佳估计`,"Give every node a best known distance from A. A itself is 0. Nothing else has been reached, so everything else starts at infinity.":`给每个节点一个已知离 A 最近的距离。A 自己是 0。其他还没到达过，所以其余的一开始都是无穷大。`,"These are guesses that can only get better. The work is improving them until they are right.":`这些估计只会越来越好。工作就是改进它们，直到它们正确为止。`,"Settle the nearest":`确定最近的`,"The unsettled node with the smallest distance is A, at 0. Nothing can be closer, so 0 is final: A is <strong>settled</strong>.":`距离最小的未确定节点是 A，为 0。不可能有更近的了，所以 0 是最终结果：A <strong>确定</strong>了。`,"Now try each edge out of A. B can be reached for 4 and C for 1, both better than infinity.":`现在试试 A 出去的每条边。B 花 4 就能到达，C 花 1，都比无穷大好。`,settled:`已确定`,"A better way round":`绕一下更好`,"The nearest unsettled node is now C, at 1, so settle it. From C, B costs 1 + 2 = 3. That beats the 4 it had, so B’s guess improves and its route changes.":`现在最近的未确定节点是 C，为 1，所以确定它。从 C 出发，B 的花费是 1 + 2 = 3。这比原来的 4 好，所以 B 的估计改进了，它的路线也变了。`,"E is reached for the first time: 1 + 7 = 8.":`E 第一次被到达：1 + 7 = 8。`,"Why settle the nearest":`为什么确定最近的`,"Every other route to it would go through something farther away first, so none can be shorter.":`通往它的其他任何路线都要先经过更远的地方，所以没有一条能更短。`,"Outwards by cost":`按代价向外扩展`,"B is next, at 3. Through B, D can be reached for 3 + 3 = 6.":`下一个是 B，为 3。经过 B，D 花 3 + 3 = 6 就能到达。`,"The settled nodes spread outwards from A in order of distance: 0, 1, 3. Next will be whichever of D and E is closer.":`已确定的节点按距离顺序从 A 向外扩展：0、1、3。下一个会是 D 和 E 中更近的那个。`,"Every distance final":`每个距离都是最终的`,"D settles at 6, and through it E improves once more: 6 + 1 = 7, beating the direct road from C. E settles last.":`D 在 6 确定，经过它，E 又改进了一次：6 + 1 = 7，胜过了从 C 直达的路。E 最后确定。`,"The coloured edges are the cheapest route to every town. The best way to E uses four roads, and two of the six roads are not used at all.":`着色的边是通往每个城镇最便宜的路线。去 E 的最好路线用了四条路，而六条路中有两条根本没用上。`,"O((V + E) log V) with a priority queue to find the nearest. Weights must not be negative.":`用优先队列找最近的节点，是 O((V + E) log V)。权重不能是负数。`,"Settled nearest first.":`最近的最先确定。`},"bellman-ford":{"repeat (number of nodes − 1) times:":`重复 (节点数 − 1) 次:`,"for each edge u → v, of weight w:":`对每个 权重为 w 的边 u → v:`,"if best[u] + w < best[v]:":`如果 best[u] + w < best[v]:`,"if any edge could still improve something:":`如果 还有边能改进什么:`,"there is a negative cycle":`就存在一个负环`,"A road that pays you":`一条倒贴钱的路`,"Dijkstra’s algorithm settles the nearest node and never looks at it again. Here it would settle B at 4, by the direct road.":`Dijkstra 算法确定了最近的节点，就再也不看它了。在这里，它会通过直达的路把 B 确定为 4。`,"But C to B costs −3. Going round by C costs 5 − 3 = 2. With a negative edge, a longer way round can turn out cheaper, and settling early is wrong.":`但 C 到 B 的花费是 −3。绕道 C 的花费是 5 − 3 = 2。有了负权边，绕远的路可能反而更便宜，过早确定就错了。`,"4, or 2?":`4，还是 2？`,Pass:`轮`,"Settle nothing":`什么都不确定`,"<strong>Bellman–Ford</strong> makes no early decisions. Start the same way: A is 0, everything else infinity.":`<strong>Bellman–Ford</strong> 不做任何过早的决定。开始的方式一样：A 是 0，其他都是无穷大。`,"Then go through <em>every edge</em>, asking one question each time: does this edge give its far end a better distance? And do that whole pass again and again.":`然后过一遍<em>每一条边</em>，每次只问一个问题：这条边能让它的另一端得到更好的距离吗？然后把这一整轮一遍又一遍地重复。`,"Pass one":`第一轮`,"B to D and C to B do nothing yet: B and C are still at infinity. A to B gives B a distance of 4. A to C gives C 5.":`B 到 D 和 C 到 B 还什么都做不了：B 和 C 还是无穷大。A 到 B 给了 B 距离 4。A 到 C 给了 C 距离 5。`,"One pass, and everything one edge from A is known.":`一轮下来，离 A 一条边的一切都知道了。`,"Pass two":`第二轮`,"B to D: 4 + 2 gives D a distance of 6. Then C to B: 5 − 3 = 2, which beats 4. B improves.":`B 到 D：4 + 2 给了 D 距离 6。然后 C 到 B：5 − 3 = 2，胜过了 4。B 改进了。`,"D’s 6 was worked out from B’s old distance, so it is now out of date. Nobody goes back to fix it. The next pass will.":`D 的 6 是根据 B 的旧距离算出来的，所以现在过时了。没有人回去修正它。下一轮会修正。`,"Pass three":`第三轮`,"B to D again: 2 + 2 = 4, better than 6. Nothing else changes.":`再次 B 到 D：2 + 2 = 4，比 6 好。其他都没变。`,"Each pass pushes correct distances one edge further out. The cheapest way to D is three edges long, so it took three passes.":`每一轮都把正确的距离再往外推一条边。去 D 最便宜的路有三条边长，所以要三轮。`,"Slow, but never fooled":`慢，但从不上当`,"A cheapest route never needs more than (nodes − 1) edges, so that many passes is always enough.":`最便宜的路线永远不需要超过 (节点数 − 1) 条边，所以这么多轮总是够的。`,"Run one extra pass. If something <em>still</em> improves, there is a loop whose total is negative: go round it for ever and the cost keeps falling. Bellman–Ford is how you find that out.":`再多跑一轮。如果<em>仍然</em>有东西改进，就存在一个总和为负的环：永远绕着它走，代价就会一直下降。Bellman–Ford 就是用来发现这一点的。`,"O(V × E). Dijkstra is much faster, so use this only when an edge can be negative.":`O(V × E)。Dijkstra 快得多，所以只在边可能为负时才用这个。`},"floyd-warshall":{"dist[i][j] ← the road from i to j, or ∞":`dist[i][j] ← 从 i 到 j 的路，或者 ∞`,"for each node k:              // one more stopover allowed":`对每个 节点 k:              // 多允许一个中转站`,"for each node i:":`对每个 节点 i:`,"for each node j:":`对每个 节点 j:`,"if dist[i][k] + dist[k][j] < dist[i][j]:":`如果 dist[i][k] + dist[k][j] < dist[i][j]:`,"Every pair at once":`一次求出每一对`,"Dijkstra and Bellman–Ford give the distances from <em>one</em> start. A route planner wants the whole table: from every town to every other.":`Dijkstra 和 Bellman–Ford 给出的是从<em>一个</em>起点出发的距离。路线规划器想要整张表：从每个城镇到其他每个城镇。`,"Start with what is certain: the direct roads. Each row is where a journey starts and each column where it ends. No road means infinity.":`先从确定的东西开始：直达的路。每一行是旅程的起点，每一列是终点。没有路就是无穷大。`,"A to B: 3":`A 到 B：3`,Roads:`道路`,"Stopovers allowed":`允许的中转站`,"Pairs with a route":`有路线的点对`,"Allow one stopover":`允许一个中转站`,"Now let journeys pass through A. For each pair, compare what is in the table with going to A and on from there.":`现在让旅程可以经过 A。对每一对，比较表里的值和先到 A 再从那里出发的路线。`,"Only D has a road into A. D to A is 2 and A to B is 3, so D to B is 5. The same way, D to C is 2 + 7 = 9.":`只有 D 有路通向 A。D 到 A 是 2，A 到 B 是 3，所以 D 到 B 是 5。同样地，D 到 C 是 2 + 7 = 9。`,"Then a second":`然后是第二个`,"Allow B as well. A to C was 7 by the direct road. Through B it is 3 + 1 = 4, so the 7 is replaced.":`再允许 B。A 到 C 走直达的路是 7。经过 B 是 3 + 1 = 4，所以 7 被替换了。`,"D to C improves too, from 9 to 6. That route goes D, A, B, C: it uses the stopover at A found a moment ago.":`D 到 C 也改进了，从 9 变成 6。这条路线是 D、A、B、C：它用到了刚才找到的经 A 中转。`,"3 + 1 beats 7":`3 + 1 胜过 7`,"And a third":`再来第三个`,"Allow C. A to C is 4 and C to D is 2, so A can reach D at last, for 6. B reaches D for 1 + 2 = 3.":`允许 C。A 到 C 是 4，C 到 D 是 2，所以 A 终于能到达 D 了，花费 6。B 到 D 花费 1 + 2 = 3。`,"Each round only ever asks one question of each pair: is it better to go through the new town?":`每一轮对每一对只问一个问题：经过新的城镇会更好吗？`,"The last town fills the table":`最后一个城镇填满了表`,"Allow D, the town with the road back to A. B to D is 3 and D to A is 2: B to A is 5. C gets to A for 4, and to B for 7.":`允许 D，也就是有路回到 A 的那个城镇。B 到 D 是 3，D 到 A 是 2：B 到 A 是 5。C 到 A 花 4，到 B 花 7。`,"Every town may now be a stopover, so every entry is a true shortest distance.":`现在每个城镇都可以作为中转站，所以每一项都是真正的最短距离。`,"Three loops":`三重循环`,"That is the whole algorithm: for each stopover, for each start, for each end, one comparison. It is dynamic programming, and the table after round k holds the best routes that use only the first k towns in between.":`这就是整个算法：对每个中转站、每个起点、每个终点，比较一次。这是动态规划，第 k 轮之后，表里存的是中间只经过前 k 个城镇的最佳路线。`,"Negative roads are fine, as long as no loop has a negative total.":`负权的路也没问题，只要没有总和为负的环。`,"O(V³) time, O(V²) memory. Good up to a few hundred nodes; beyond that, run Dijkstra from each one.":`O(V³) 时间，O(V²) 内存。几百个节点以内很好用；超过的话，就从每个节点各跑一次 Dijkstra。`},"union-find":{"while x has a parent:":`当 x 有父节点:`,"x ← its parent":`x ← 它的父节点`,"return x                 // the root names the group":`返回 x                 // 根就是组的名字`,"if a ≠ b: make a the parent of b":`如果 a ≠ b: 让 a 成为 b 的父节点`,"find, with path compression(x):":`带路径压缩的 find(x):`,"point everything on the way straight at root":`让路上的一切都直接指向 root`,"return root":`返回 root`,"Who is with whom":`谁和谁在一起`,"Are these two connected?":`这两个连通吗？`,"Connections arrive one at a time: A with B, C with D… At any moment you may be asked whether two items are connected, directly or through others.":`连接一个一个地到来：A 和 B，C 和 D……任何时候你都可能被问到两个项是否连通，不管是直接的还是通过别的项。`,"Searching the graph for every question is too slow. <strong>Union-find</strong> keeps track of the groups themselves. To begin with, every item is a group of one.":`每个问题都去搜索一遍图太慢了。<strong>并查集</strong>直接记录这些组本身。一开始，每个项都是只有自己的一组。`,"Each item is its own group.":`每个项各自一组。`,Union:`合并`,"To join two groups, point one item at the other. B now points at A; D at C; F at E.":`要合并两个组，就让一个项指向另一个。现在 B 指向 A；D 指向 C；F 指向 E。`,"An item that points at nothing is a <strong>root</strong>, and the root is the name of its group. Three roots, so three groups.":`不指向任何东西的项是<strong>根</strong>，根就是它所在组的名字。三个根，所以有三个组。`,Find:`查找`,"Which group is D in? Follow its arrow until there are no more: D leads to C, and C is a root. D’s group is C.":`D 在哪个组？沿着它的箭头走，直到没有箭头为止：D 通向 C，而 C 是根。D 的组是 C。`,"B’s arrow leads to A. Different roots, so B and D are <strong>not</strong> connected. That is the whole test.":`B 的箭头通向 A。根不同，所以 B 和 D <strong>不</strong>连通。整个检查就是这样。`,"D is in group C":`D 在组 C 中`,"Join two groups":`合并两个组`,"Now connect B and D. Find both roots, A and C, and point one at the other.":`现在连接 B 和 D。找到两者的根 A 和 C，让一个指向另一个。`,"One arrow moved four items into the same group. Nobody was relabelled: B and D never pointed at each other, and they are connected all the same.":`移动一个箭头，就把四个项放进了同一个组。没有谁被重新标记：B 和 D 从没互相指向过，但它们照样连通了。`,"The chains grow":`链在变长`,"Ask about D again. Its path to the root is now two arrows long: D, C, A.":`再问一次 D。它到根的路径现在有两个箭头长：D、C、A。`,"Every union can make some paths longer. Left alone, a group can become one long chain, and find slows to a walk.":`每次合并都可能让某些路径变长。放任不管的话，一个组可能变成一条长链，查找就慢得像在步行。`,"D is in group A":`D 在组 A 中`,"Path compression":`路径压缩`,"Speed-up":`提速`,"The fix costs almost nothing. Having walked from D to the root, point D <em>straight at it</em>. Next time, D is one step from the answer.":`修复几乎不花什么代价。从 D 走到根之后，让 D <em>直接指向它</em>。下次 D 离答案只有一步。`,"Each find flattens the path it used, so the trees stay shallow by themselves.":`每次查找都会把它走过的路径压平，所以树会自己保持很浅。`,"With this and one more small trick, find and union are as good as O(1) each.":`有了这个再加一个小技巧，查找和合并每次都几乎等于 O(1)。`,"one step from its root":`离它的根只有一步`,"Used for networks, clustering, and building spanning trees.":`用于网络、聚类，以及构建生成树。`},"minimum-spanning-trees":{"sort the edges, cheapest first":`把边排序，最便宜的在前`,"for each edge, in that order:":`对每个 边，按那个顺序:`,"if its two ends are not yet connected:":`如果 它的两端还没有连通:`,"keep the edge          // union":`保留这条边          // 合并`,"// otherwise it would close a loop: skip it":`// 否则它会形成环：跳过`,"stop when every node is connected":`当每个节点都连通时停止`,"Kruskal’s algorithm":`Kruskal 算法`,"Connect everything, cheaply":`便宜地连起一切`,"Five towns need joining to one network. Cable can be laid along any road, at the cost shown. Which roads should be used so that every town is connected and the total is as small as possible?":`五个城镇需要连成一个网络。电缆可以沿任何一条路铺设，代价如图所示。应该用哪些路，才能让每个城镇都连通，并且总代价尽可能小？`,"The answer never contains a loop, since a loop always has one cable too many. So it is a tree that reaches every node: a <strong>minimum spanning tree</strong>.":`答案里永远不会有环，因为环总是多了一根电缆。所以它是一棵到达每个节点的树：<strong>最小生成树</strong>。`,"Edges, cheapest first":`边，最便宜的在前`,"Cable laid":`已铺电缆`,"Cheapest edge first":`最便宜的边优先`,"Sort the roads by cost and take them in order. The two cheapest cost 1 each: A to C, and D to E. Neither closes a loop, so both are kept.":`把路按代价排序，按顺序取。最便宜的两条各花 1：A 到 C，D 到 E。两条都不形成环，所以都保留。`,"There are now two separate groups, and B on its own.":`现在有两个分开的组，B 单独一个。`,"Keep taking the cheapest":`继续取最便宜的`,"Next is C to B, at 2. B was not connected to anything, so the edge is kept. Then B to D, at 3: its ends are in different groups, so it joins them.":`下一条是 C 到 B，花 2。B 还没和任何东西连通，所以保留这条边。然后是 B 到 D，花 3：它的两端在不同的组里，所以它把两组连了起来。`,"Every town can now reach every other.":`现在每个城镇都能到达其他每个城镇了。`,"Skip anything that closes a loop":`跳过任何会形成环的边`,"A to B costs 4, but A and B are already connected through C. Adding it would only make a loop. Skip it. The same goes for C to E.":`A 到 B 花 4，但 A 和 B 已经通过 C 连通了。加上它只会形成一个环。跳过。C 到 E 也一样。`,"“Are these two already connected?” is exactly what union-find answers, which is why the two are used together.":`“这两个已经连通了吗？”正是并查集回答的问题，所以两者总是一起用。`,"A–B would close a loop":`A–B 会形成环`,"The cheapest network":`最便宜的网络`,"Four edges join five towns, for a total of 7. No other choice of roads connects everything for less.":`四条边连起了五个城镇，总计 7。没有其他选路的方法能以更低的代价连起一切。`,"Always taking the cheapest safe edge is a <strong>greedy</strong> method, and here greed is provably right.":`总是取最便宜的安全边，这是一种<strong>贪心</strong>方法，而在这里，贪心被证明是对的。`,"O(E log E), nearly all of it the sorting.":`O(E log E)，几乎全花在排序上。`,"n towns always need n − 1 cables.":`n 个城镇总是需要 n − 1 根电缆。`},"prims-algorithm":{"while some node is outside the tree:":`当 还有节点在树外:`,"pick the cheapest edge that joins":`选出最便宜的、连接`,"a node inside to a node outside":`树内节点和树外节点的边`,"add that edge, and its outside node,":`把这条边和它的树外节点`,"to the tree":`加进树里`,"The tree":`树`,"Grow one tree":`长一棵树`,"Kruskal built the spanning tree out of the cheapest edges wherever they were, and let the pieces join up. <strong>Prim’s algorithm</strong> reaches the same tree another way: start from one node and grow outward.":`Kruskal 用最便宜的边构建生成树，不管它们在哪里，再让各部分连起来。<strong>Prim 算法</strong>用另一种方法得到同样的树：从一个节点开始，向外生长。`,"At every step the tree is a single connected piece. The only question is which edge to grow along next.":`每一步树都是一个连通的整体。唯一的问题是接下来沿着哪条边生长。`,"start anywhere":`从任何地方开始`,"In the tree":`在树中`,"Edges kept":`已保留的边`,"Cost so far":`目前的代价`,"The cheapest edge leaving the tree":`离开树的最便宜的边`,"Two roads leave A: 4 to B, 1 to C. Take the cheaper, and C joins the tree.":`从 A 出去有两条路：到 B 花 4，到 C 花 1。取更便宜的，C 加入树。`,"The number over each outside node is the cheapest road linking it to the tree so far. B has just improved: 2 through C beats 4 from A. D cannot be reached yet.":`每个树外节点上方的数字，是目前把它连到树上的最便宜的路。B 刚刚改进了：经 C 的 2 胜过从 A 出发的 4。D 还到不了。`,"Again, from the whole tree":`再来，从整棵树出发`,"The cheapest way out of the tree is now the 2 to B. Take it.":`现在离开树最便宜的路是到 B 的 2。取它。`,"A–B is left with both ends inside, so it can never be used: it would only close a loop. Through B, D comes within reach at 3.":`A–B 的两端都在树里了，所以它永远用不上：它只会形成环。经过 B，D 可以用 3 到达了。`,"A better offer turns up":`出现了更好的报价`,"D is nearer than E: 3 against 7. D joins.":`D 比 E 近：3 对 7。D 加入。`,"And D has a road to E that costs only 1. E’s number drops from 7 to 1.":`而且 D 有一条到 E 的路只花 1。E 的数字从 7 降到 1。`,"Everyone is in":`全都进来了`,"E joins by the 1. No node is left outside, so the tree is finished: four edges, total cost 7.":`E 通过 1 加入。没有节点留在树外了，所以树完成了：四条边，总代价 7。`,"It is exactly the tree Kruskal found. Both methods are guaranteed a cheapest tree. Where several trees tie they may pick different ones, but the total always comes out the same.":`这正是 Kruskal 找到的那棵树。两种方法都保证得到一棵最便宜的树。当几棵树代价相同时，它们可能选出不同的树，但总代价总是一样的。`,"Dijkstra’s cousin":`Dijkstra 的近亲`,"Keep the outside nodes in a min-heap, ordered by their number, and each step is a pop followed by a few updates.":`把树外节点按它们的数字放进一个最小堆，每一步就是一次弹出，再加几次更新。`,"That is Dijkstra’s algorithm with one change. Dijkstra’s number is the distance from the <em>start</em>. Prim’s is the distance from the <em>tree</em>.":`这就是只改了一处的 Dijkstra 算法。Dijkstra 的数字是离<em>起点</em>的距离。Prim 的是离<em>树</em>的距离。`,"O(E log V) with a heap, the same as Kruskal. Prim needs no sorting and no union-find.":`用堆是 O(E log V)，和 Kruskal 一样。Prim 不需要排序，也不需要并查集。`}};export{n as default,e as resizing,t as tries};